    #      record's families are derived from the --parts lines, the removal
    #      record's from its entries table, which the rule checked row by row
    #      (the rulings allow a row recompressed or changed); six record files
    #      installed, four when the keep is skipped.
    #  VK. UK stands: this script runs no `rm -rf`; the sourced
    #      scripts/counting.sh, a committed script, runs one on the directory its
    #      counting controls make (allowed: a directory the script created in
    #      that run); the working directory and the keeps stand, kept, and
    #      Python writes no bytecode.
    #
    #
    #
    # CARRIED TO M3 part 6 P3 from M3 part 6 P2's run script (at the phase
    # commit d3c4a9c, printed in records/logs/m3p6-p2/run.log; its change lists
    # up to VK are above), generated by <home>/.cache/emend-build/m3p6-p3/gen/
    # run.py, every replacement asserted to occur as often as it says, the top
    # summary and the body from the survey to the corpus record pairs'
    # installation replaced whole (gen/run_block.sh, by its anchor lines, P2's
    # record check carried into it unchanged), and the body grepped afterwards
    # for P2's names, subjects, stems and the tokens imgcmp, imgsurvey,
    # m3p6-p2-, P1_REC and PREV_CB. What differs, and why:
    #  XA. The phase, the log directory, the subjects, the script directory
    #      (<scripts>, <home>/.cache/emend-build/m3p6-p3/scripts, on the disk)
    #      and the keep (m3p6-p3/keep-host) are this phase's; the base is P2's
    #      record commit ("M3 part 6 P2 record:"); the phase commit is P3's tool
    #      commit by its subject ("M3 part 6 P3: emend-copy --copy-sample"); one
    #      sample, copy, with its run directory <runs>/<date>-<sha>-copy and its
    #      record stem m3p6-p3-<date>-<sha> (the spec's name), and three rerun
    #      directories <runs>/<date>-<sha>-anchor, -removeimage and -commentbox
    #      (RERUNS); SUPERSEDED_RUN names the four by their common stem; the
    #      spec pinned through SPEC_SHA at P3's doc commit, planning's rulings
    #      during P3 standing uncommitted in the working tree's copy, printed.
    #  XB. Change VB's form: the committed open-check record the keep is
    #      compared with is P2's, the last committed, named by its record
    #      commit, resolved by its subject ("M3 part 6 P2 record:"; no hash is
    #      typed here); it is the base itself, the parent of P3's doc commit; the
    #      control names the doc commit instead. P2_REC names the same commit, the
    #      one whose run directories the reruns are compared with (change XF).
    #  XC. The comparison is copycmp.py, built for this phase (<home>/.cache/
    #      emend-build/m3p6-p3/gen/copycmp_build.py) with P2's imgcmp.py
    #      readers copied by name, one mode, copy, fifteen flags: whole_bytes,
    #      data_same, kept_same, views_same, setup_same, dropped_gone (the
    #      spec's copy check, and the copy built from S byte for byte),
    #      rels_set (ruling 1), comments_same and notes_placed (the spec's
    #      carried checks), workbook_sheet, types_set, chain_rule, rest_same,
    #      xml_values and flagged (P2's). The lines' relations are the spec's:
    #      one sheet more, the copy's counts its source's, no chain after a
    #      formula. The tool's counts equal the comparison's.
    #  XD. NEW, the survey (copysurvey.py, <scripts>, copied into <work> and
    #      printed) replaces VD's, in its form: <corpus> its parameter, every
    #      regular file of <corpus>/corpus listed, one wb line of twenty fields
    #      per workbook; the log checks its forms, prints the distributions and
    #      checks every line's figures against it, and the comparison's parts
    #      against it. No drawings line (no decision rests on one here).
    #  XE. Changes PE, QE, SE and VE (every row ok) stand. The entries rule is
    #      the rulings during P3's: the copy's entry added; its rels part added
    #      exactly when S has a hyperlink or a comments relationship (ruling 1);
    #      the comments and VML parts added when carried; the workbook part, its
    #      rels part and the content types changed, flagged descriptor at most;
    #      the chain's entry dropped exactly when S holds a formula and the
    #      workbook a chain; every other row identical and unflagged; nothing
    #      recompressed. Each allowance has a control that accepts it where it
    #      applies and one that refuses it where it does not. The summary's
    #      totals are checked against what the rows imply and against the
    #      entries table.
    #  XF. NEW, the three earlier samples once more on both targets, their
    #      outputs by sha256, their lines and their diff tables P2's runs' byte
    #      for byte (change VF's form for three samples), the run directories
    #      read from the "the run directories:" line of P2's run log at P2's
    #      record commit and checked against the run directory P2's committed
    #      anchor record names; no record pair is written for the reruns.
    #  XG. Change UG's no-row rule gives way: the copy makes the write a formula
    #      change when S holds a formula (specs/0013's rule, "The copy"), so
    #      each chain workbook's calcChain row is dropped exactly there, and is
    #      identical and unflagged elsewhere; some row is dropped.
    #  XH. Change PH (the open check's own TMPDIR device) stands, unchanged.
    #  XI. The plants: every flag's planted control runs on the first ok
    #      workbook in manifest order of the plain case (S's comments not
    #      carried) and of the carried case, each on its own check line, the
    #      plant turning its own flag; every flag has a plant on both cases.
    #      The xml values check wants some value written (the workbook's new
    #      sheet; change LF's form).
    #  XJ. The run loop, the record pair, the keep and the open check are VJ's
    #      with this phase's names; the record's families are derived from its
    #      entries table, which the rule checked row by row; four record files
    #      installed, two when the keep is skipped.
    #  XK. Ruling 8 of the planning rulings during P2 (build pruning) and
    #      ruling 10 of the planning rulings during P3 (one target root per
    #      phase, one subdirectory per source tree): the phase's target root is
    #      <target>, <home>/.cache/emend-build/m3p6-p3/target, and every build
    #      of <repo> by this script, dry or logged, goes into <target>/main
    #      (CARGO_TARGET_DIR), the subdirectory ruling 10 gives the main tree;
    #      this script builds from no other tree. P2's <build> placeholder (a
    #      run directory holding its own target) is gone with the input
    #      RUN_BUILD_ROOT, so no run moves the builds, and nothing here cleans
    #      them; the i686 keep is <work>/keep-i686, kept, not under the target.
    #      VK stands: this script runs no `rm -rf`.
    #
    # Usage: m5p1-p1-run.sh <phase commit> > <file outside the tree>; the caller
    # moves the output to records/logs/m5p1-p1/run.log.
    set -uo pipefail
    SELF_DIR=$(cd "$(dirname "$0")" && pwd)
    SELF=$SELF_DIR/$(basename "$0")
    # specs/0017 P1 verification ruling 7: this script's own standard error, kept and counted at the end.
    mkdir -p "$SELF_DIR/out" || exit 2
    ERR=$SELF_DIR/out/run.stderr
    exec 2>"$ERR"
    cd "$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)" || exit 2
    MAIN=$(pwd)
    
    C=${1:?phase commit required}
    # Every environment input, as it was set, before any is unset.
    INPUT_NAMES="RUN_SUFFIX SUPERSEDED_RUN SUPERSEDED_KEEP RERUN_NOTE RERUN_FILES RECORDS_DEST RUN_KEEP RUN_OUT_ROOT RUN_SKIP_KEEP EMEND_CORPUS_DIR EMEND_KEEP_DIR HOME"
    declare -A INPUT_SEEN
    for v in $INPUT_NAMES; do
      if [ -n "${!v+x}" ]; then INPUT_SEEN[$v]=${!v}; else INPUT_SEEN[$v]=unset; fi
    done
    CORPUS=${EMEND_CORPUS_DIR:-$HOME/emend-testing}
    export RUSTUP_AUTO_INSTALL=0 CARGO_TERM_COLOR=never CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=4
    # Python writes no bytecode, so nothing arises to be removed.
    export PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1
    unset EMEND_KEEP_DIR EMEND_CORPUS_DIR RUSTDOCFLAGS RUSTFLAGS
    IMAGE=localhost/emend-lo:25.2.3-2-deb13u6
    LO_TIMEOUT_S=600
    SPEC=specs/0032-read-breadth-styles.md
    # Change NSA: the committed blob the doc commit holds (FACTS.md "Spec pins",
    # pasted from sha256sum).
    SPEC_WANT=9f9c12c93a36bf040a9229b314b47733c8390273ca601c096b76e5ee3f8a25bd
    SAMPLE=namedstyles
    EDIT=--namedstyles-sample
    PHASE_DIR=$HOME/.cache/emend-build/m5p1-p1
    # Change NSK: every build of <repo>, dry or logged, goes into the main tree's
    # subdirectory of the phase's one target root, <target>/main; no input moves
    # it and nothing here cleans it. The logged run leaves RUN_KEEP unset; a dry
    # run points it elsewhere so it leaves no keep where the logged run refuses
    # one.
    TARGET_ROOT=$PHASE_DIR/target
    BUILD_ROOT=$TARGET_ROOT/main
    KEEP=${RUN_KEEP:-$PHASE_DIR/keep-host}
    RUN_OUT_ROOT=${RUN_OUT_ROOT:-$CORPUS/runs}
    RUN_SKIP_KEEP=${RUN_SKIP_KEEP:-no}
    case $RUN_SKIP_KEEP in yes | no) ;; *) echo "RUN_SKIP_KEEP is yes or no" >&2; exit 2 ;; esac
    INSTALLED=()
    I686=i686-unknown-linux-musl
    RECORDS_DEST=${RECORDS_DEST:-records}
    # A keep in place is another attempt's, moved below once the header can list
    # it; without SUPERSEDED_KEEP naming the attempt it is refused.
    SUPERSEDED_KEEP=${SUPERSEDED_KEEP:-}
    case $SUPERSEDED_KEEP in '' | attempt-[1-9]) ;; *) echo "SUPERSEDED_KEEP is attempt-<n> or nothing" >&2; exit 2 ;; esac
    if [ "$RUN_SKIP_KEEP" = no ] && [ -e "$KEEP" ] && [ -z "$SUPERSEDED_KEEP" ]; then echo "$KEEP is already there; name its attempt in SUPERSEDED_KEEP" >&2; exit 2; fi
    mkdir -p "$BUILD_ROOT" || exit 2
    export CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$BUILD_ROOT
    RECORDS=$SELF_DIR/out/records
    # The working directory is on the disk under <scripts>/out and kept; nothing
    # here is removed.
    B=$(mktemp -d "$SELF_DIR/out/work.XXXXXX") || exit 2
    # Change NSB: the counting library is the phase commit's, by git show.
    git show "$C:scripts/counting.sh" >"$B/counting.sh" || exit 2
    . "$B/counting.sh"
    fail=0
    check() { echo "  $1: $2"; [ "$2" = yes ] || fail=1; }
    yn() { if "$@"; then echo yes; else echo no; fi; }
    # For a condition that must NOT hold: a leading bang inside yn runs a
    # command named by the bang (specs/0001), so a negation has its own helper.
    ynnot() { if "$@"; then echo no; else echo yes; fi; }
    TAB=$(printf '\t')
    sha_of() { sha256sum <"$1" | cut -d' ' -f1; }
    
    head_is() { [ "$(git rev-parse HEAD)" = "$1" ]; }
    full_sha() { printf '%s' "$1" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -qE '^[0-9a-f]{40}$'; }
    # The given commit is the phase commit when it is a full sha and HEAD.
    given_ok() { full_sha "$1" && head_is "$1"; }
    if given_ok "$C"; then :; else echo "the phase commit must be a full 40-hex sha that is HEAD, not $C" >&2; exit 2; fi
    NULL_SHA=0000000000000000000000000000000000000000
    case "${C: -1}" in 0) LAST=1 ;; *) LAST=0 ;; esac
    FAKE_SHA=${C:0:39}$LAST
    SHORT=$(git rev-parse --short=7 "$C")
    DATE=$(date -u +%Y-%m-%d)
    # What the status pattern admits (change NSB): this phase's log directory,
    # this phase's two record pairs (named by the run's date and the phase
    # commit's short sha, untracked) and planning's modified specs/0032; nothing
    # else.
    OURS="^((\\?\\?| ?[MARCD]) records/logs/m5p1-p1/|\\?\\? records/m5p1-(p1|open)-$DATE-$SHORT[.](md|txt)\$| M specs/0032-read-breadth-styles[.]md\$)"
    entry_all=$(run_lines git status --porcelain)
    entry_ours=$(run_matches -E "$OURS" git status --porcelain)
    entry_clean() { [ "$entry_all" != error ] && [ "$entry_ours" != error ] && [ "$entry_all" = "$entry_ours" ]; }
    if entry_clean; then :; else
      echo "the working tree holds changes outside this phase's logs, records and planning's spec" >&2
      exit 2
    fi
    STEM=m5p1-p1-$DATE-$SHORT
    STEM_OPEN=m5p1-open-$DATE-$SHORT
    # A rerun takes a suffix, so its run directory is never the superseded one.
    RUN_SUFFIX=${RUN_SUFFIX:-}
    case $RUN_SUFFIX in '' | -[b-z]) ;; *) echo "RUN_SUFFIX is -b to -z or nothing" >&2; exit 2 ;; esac
    RUN=$DATE-$SHORT$RUN_SUFFIX
    O=$RUN_OUT_ROOT/$RUN-$SAMPLE
    mkdir -p "$RECORDS" "$RECORDS_DEST" || exit 2
    # A rerun names the superseded run directory, which is MOVED into
    # <scripts>/out/superseded after the header prints it, never removed; it
    # must be another run of this phase, not this one.
    SUPERSEDED_RUN=${SUPERSEDED_RUN:-}
    case $SUPERSEDED_RUN in
      '' | 20[0-9][0-9]-[01][0-9]-[0-3][0-9]-[0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f] | 20[0-9][0-9]-[01][0-9]-[0-3][0-9]-[0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f]-[b-z]) ;;
      *) echo "SUPERSEDED_RUN is not a run directory's name" >&2; exit 2 ;;
    esac
    if [ -n "$SUPERSEDED_RUN" ] && [ "$SUPERSEDED_RUN" = "$RUN" ]; then echo "SUPERSEDED_RUN names this run's own directory" >&2; exit 2; fi
    for f in "$RECORDS/$STEM_OPEN.md" "$RECORDS/$STEM_OPEN.txt" "$RECORDS_DEST/$STEM_OPEN.md" "$RECORDS_DEST/$STEM_OPEN.txt" \
             "$RECORDS/$STEM.md" "$RECORDS/$STEM.txt" "$RECORDS_DEST/$STEM.md" "$RECORDS_DEST/$STEM.txt"; do
      if [ -e "$f" ]; then echo "$f is already there; move it aside first" >&2; exit 2; fi
    done
    # A run directory that exists before the run is another attempt's; refused
    # (the runner itself refuses one holding an earlier run's conversion
    # directories, specs/0030 decision 1 A).
    if [ -e "$O" ]; then echo "$O is already there; name a fresh run" >&2; exit 2; fi
    
    # The corpus's path begins with <repo>'s, so <runs> and <corpus> are
    # replaced before <repo> (M4 part 1 P3's order); the phase's directories
    # before <phase>, and <home> last.
    scrub() {
      sed -e "s#$B#<work>#g" -e "s#$SELF_DIR#<scripts>#g" -e "s#$KEEP#<keep>#g" \
        -e "s#$TARGET_ROOT#<target>#g" -e "s#$RUN_OUT_ROOT#<runs>#g" -e "s#$CORPUS#<corpus>#g" \
        -e "s#$MAIN#<repo>#g" -e "s#$PHASE_DIR#<phase>#g" -e "s#$HOME#<home>#g"
    }
    exec 3>&1
    exec > >(scrub >&3)
    SCRUB_PID=$!
    
    echo "command: git rev-parse HEAD"
    echo "invocation: bash <scripts>/$(basename "$0") $*"
    echo "about: M5 part 1 P1 phase commit $C; HEAD at run: $(git rev-parse HEAD)"
    # The environment inputs, each on its labelled line.
    for v in $INPUT_NAMES; do echo "input: $v=${INPUT_SEEN[$v]}"; done
    echo "input: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY: $([ -n "${ANTHROPIC_API_KEY:-}" ] && echo set || echo unset) (its value never printed)"
    echo
    echo "## the three shape greps, over this script, before its log (specs/0001)"
    D='$'
    SHAPE_CHAIN="\\${D}\\((yn|ynnot|is|isnot) .*(&&|\\|\\|)"
    SHAPE_BANG="\\${D}\\((yn|ynnot|is|isnot) !"
    SHAPE_ASSIGN="\\${D}\\((yn|ynnot|is|isnot) [A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*="
    printf '%s\n' "x=${D}(is [ 1 ] && true)" "y=${D}(isnot ! true)" "z=${D}(yn N=1 true)" >"$B/shape-fixture"
    echo "command: count_matches -E <shape> <this script>, and the same over a fixture holding one line of each shape"
    for shape in CHAIN BANG ASSIGN; do
      var=SHAPE_$shape
      n_self=$(count_matches -E "${!var}" "$SELF")
      n_fix=$(count_matches -E "${!var}" "$B/shape-fixture")
      echo "  shape $shape: in this script $n_self; in the fixture $n_fix"
      check "$shape: this script holds none" "$(yn [ "$n_self" = 0 ])"
      check "control: $shape: the same form finds the fixture's one line" "$(yn [ "$n_fix" = 1 ])"
    done
    check "control: ynnot reports no on a passing command" "$(yn [ "$(ynnot true)" = no ])"
    
    echo
    echo "## the phase's commits by role, read from git"
    by_subject() { git log --format='%H' -n 1 -F --grep="$1"; }
    REC=$(by_subject 'M4 part 2 close-out record: the push, the CI run and the scan')
    DOC=$(by_subject 'M5 part 1 P1: commit planning docs (the M4 part 2 close-out rulings, the Milestone 5 outline, specs/0032)')
    CRATE=$(by_subject 'M5 part 1 P1: named styles, differential styles and the default font read typed')
    CODE=$(by_subject 'M5 part 1 P1: emend-copy --namedstyles-sample')
    # Change NSF: the record the keep is compared with, named by its record
    # commit, resolved by its subject (no hash is typed here), and checked below.
    PREV_OPEN_REC=$(by_subject 'M3 part 7 P5 record: logs, the sample records, the open record, the independent check')
    echo "command: git log --format=%H -n 1 -F --grep=<the role's subject>, for each role"
    echo "  M4 part 2's close-out record commit (the base): ${REC:-none}"
    echo "  the doc commit: ${DOC:-none}"
    echo "  the crate commit: ${CRATE:-none}"
    echo "  the tool commit, the phase commit: ${CODE:-none}"
    echo "  M3 part 7 P5's record commit, the last to add an open-check record, named by its commit (change NSF): ${PREV_OPEN_REC:-none}"
    echo "command: git rev-parse <phase commit>~0 to <phase commit>~3"
    for k in 0 1 2 3; do git rev-parse "$C~$k"; done | sed 's/^/    /'
    roles_in_order() {
      local r k=0
      for r in "$CODE" "$CRATE" "$DOC" "$REC"; do
        [ -n "$r" ] || return 1
        [ "$(git rev-parse "$C~$k")" = "$r" ] || return 1
        k=$((k + 1))
      done
    }
    check "the tool commit, the crate commit, the doc commit and the base, each the next one's parent, the tool commit the phase commit (change NSA)" "$(yn roles_in_order)"
    roles_ctl() { local CODE=$CRATE; roles_in_order; }
    check "control: roles_in_order refuses the crate commit named as the phase commit" "$(ynnot roles_ctl)"
    roles_ctl2() { local REC=$DOC; roles_in_order; }
    check "control: roles_in_order refuses the doc commit named as the base" "$(ynnot roles_ctl2)"
    echo "command: git log -1 --format=%s <M3 part 7 P5's record commit>"
    echo "    $(git log -1 --format=%s "$PREV_OPEN_REC")"
    prev_is_record() { [ -n "$PREV_OPEN_REC" ] && git cat-file -e "$PREV_OPEN_REC^{commit}" && [ "$(git log -1 --format=%s "$PREV_OPEN_REC" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -cE '^M3 part 7 P5 record: ')" = 1 ] && git merge-base --is-ancestor "$PREV_OPEN_REC" "$C"; }
    check "the named record commit is M3 part 7 P5's record commit, an ancestor of the phase commit" "$(yn prev_is_record)"
    prev_ctl() { local PREV_OPEN_REC=$DOC; prev_is_record; }
    check "control: the same check refuses the doc commit named instead" "$(ynnot prev_ctl)"
    echo "  the phase commit given to this script: $C"
    echo "  git rev-parse HEAD at this run:        $(git rev-parse HEAD)"
    echo "  the controls' commits: the null commit $NULL_SHA; the fabricated commit $FAKE_SHA (the given one, its last hex digit changed); the short sha $SHORT"
    check "the phase commit given to this script is a full sha" "$(yn full_sha "$C")"
    check "the phase commit given to this script is HEAD" "$(yn head_is "$C")"
    check "the phase commit is the tool commit, by its subject" "$(yn [ "$CODE" = "$C" ])"
    check "control: the same comparison refuses the null commit" "$(ynnot given_ok "$NULL_SHA")"
    check "control: the same comparison refuses a fabricated commit" "$(ynnot given_ok "$FAKE_SHA")"
    check "control: the same comparison refuses a short sha of the real commit" "$(ynnot given_ok "$SHORT")"
    short_names_head() { [ "$(git rev-parse "$SHORT")" = "$(git rev-parse HEAD)" ]; }
    check "control: the short sha is the real commit's, so only its form is refused" "$(yn short_names_head)"
    echo "phase: Milestone 5 part 1 P1 ($SPEC) run.log; run at $(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)"
    if [ -n "${RERUN_NOTE:-}" ]; then
      echo "rerun: $RERUN_NOTE"
      echo "command: sha256sum and wc -c over each superseded attempt named above, with the directory it is kept in"
      for sf in ${RERUN_FILES:-}; do
        if [ -f "$sf" ]; then
          printf '    %s  %s bytes  %s  kept in %s\n' "$(sha256sum "$sf" | cut -d' ' -f1)" "$(wc -c <"$sf")" "$(basename "$sf")" "$(dirname "$sf")"
        else
          printf '    NO HASH EXISTS for %s: the file is not there at run time (named in %s)\n' "$(basename "$sf")" "$(dirname "$sf")"
        fi
      done
      if [ -z "${RERUN_FILES:-}" ]; then echo "    RERUN_FILES was not set, so no attempt above is hashed by this run"; fi
    fi
    
    # The two move checks as functions, run over planted inputs every time
    # below, and over a real moved keep or run directory when there is one.
    # keep_pairs_ok <listing>: the .in.xlsx lines times two equal the listing's
    # lines (the pattern in double quotes so the tab is interpolated).
    keep_pairs_ok() {
      local pairs files
      pairs=$(count_matches -E "[.]in[.]xlsx${TAB}" "$1")
      files=$(count_lines "$1")
      [ "$files" -ge 2 ] && [ "$((pairs * 2))" = "$files" ]
    }
    # run_listing <dir> <listing>: the listing of a run directory, one line per
    # file, path and bytes.
    run_listing() { (cd "$1" && find . -type f -printf '%P\t%s\n' | LC_ALL=C sort) >"$2"; }
    # run_listing_ok <dir> <listing>: the listing names each file once and at
    # least one.
    run_listing_ok() {
      local files lines uniq
      files=$(find "$1" -type f | wc -l)
      lines=$(count_lines "$2")
      uniq=$(cut -f1 "$2" | LC_ALL=C sort -u | count_lines /dev/stdin)
      [ "$files" -ge 1 ] && [ "$lines" = "$files" ] && [ "$uniq" = "$files" ]
    }
    
    if [ -n "$SUPERSEDED_RUN" ]; then
      SUP_OUT=$RUN_OUT_ROOT/$SUPERSEDED_RUN-$SAMPLE
      SUP_TO=$SELF_DIR/out/superseded/run-$SUPERSEDED_RUN-$SAMPLE
      echo "the superseded run directory, moved before this run: <runs>/$SUPERSEDED_RUN-$SAMPLE to <scripts>/out/superseded/run-$SUPERSEDED_RUN-$SAMPLE"
      if [ -d "$SUP_OUT" ]; then
        echo "command: sha256sum <runs>/$SUPERSEDED_RUN-$SAMPLE/summary.host.tsv and summary.i686.tsv; mv <runs>/$SUPERSEDED_RUN-$SAMPLE <scripts>/out/superseded/run-$SUPERSEDED_RUN-$SAMPLE"
        for sl in host i686; do
          if [ -f "$SUP_OUT/summary.$sl.tsv" ]; then echo "    summary.$sl.tsv sha256 $(sha_of "$SUP_OUT/summary.$sl.tsv")"; else echo "    summary.$sl.tsv: NO HASH EXISTS, the file is not there"; fi
        done
        run_listing "$SUP_OUT" "$B/superseded-run.listing"
        echo "command: (cd <runs>/$SUPERSEDED_RUN-$SAMPLE && find . -type f -printf '%P<tab>%s<newline>' | LC_ALL=C sort) | sha256sum"
        echo "    files $(find "$SUP_OUT" -type f | wc -l); listing lines $(count_lines "$B/superseded-run.listing"); listing sha256 $(sha_of "$B/superseded-run.listing")"
        check "the listing of $SUPERSEDED_RUN-$SAMPLE names each of its files once" "$(yn run_listing_ok "$SUP_OUT" "$B/superseded-run.listing")"
        if [ -e "$SUP_TO" ]; then echo "    $SUP_TO is already there"; fail=1; else mkdir -p "$SELF_DIR/out/superseded" && mv "$SUP_OUT" "$SUP_TO"; fi
      fi
      sup_moved() { [ ! -e "$SUP_OUT" ] && [ -d "$SUP_TO" ]; }
      check "the superseded run directory $SUPERSEDED_RUN-$SAMPLE is moved, not removed, before the run" "$(yn sup_moved)"
    fi
    if [ -n "$SUPERSEDED_KEEP" ]; then
      KEEP_TO=$SELF_DIR/out/superseded/keep-$SUPERSEDED_KEEP
      echo "the superseded keep, moved before this run: <keep> to <scripts>/out/superseded/keep-$SUPERSEDED_KEEP"
      if [ -d "$KEEP" ]; then
        (cd "$KEEP" && find . -type f -printf '%P\t%s\n' | LC_ALL=C sort) >"$B/superseded-keep.listing"
        echo "command: (cd <keep> && find . -type f -printf '%P<tab>%s<newline>' | LC_ALL=C sort) | sha256sum; the .in.xlsx files counted; mv <keep> <scripts>/out/superseded/keep-$SUPERSEDED_KEEP"
        echo "    pairs $(count_matches -E "[.]in[.]xlsx${TAB}" "$B/superseded-keep.listing"); files $(count_lines "$B/superseded-keep.listing"); listing sha256 $(sha_of "$B/superseded-keep.listing")"
        check "the moved keep's pairs times two equals its files" "$(yn keep_pairs_ok "$B/superseded-keep.listing")"
        if [ -e "$KEEP_TO" ]; then echo "    $KEEP_TO is already there"; fail=1; else mkdir -p "$SELF_DIR/out/superseded" && mv "$KEEP" "$KEEP_TO"; fi
      else
        echo "    NO LISTING EXISTS: there is no keep in place to move"
      fi
      keep_moved() { [ ! -e "$KEEP" ] && [ -d "$KEEP_TO" ]; }
      check "the superseded keep is moved, not removed, before the run" "$(yn keep_moved)"
    fi
    echo "superseded run directory named: ${SUPERSEDED_RUN:-none}; superseded keep named: ${SUPERSEDED_KEEP:-none}"
    echo
    echo "## the two move checks over planted inputs, run every time"
    printf 'x.1.in.xlsx%s1\nx.1.out.xlsx%s1\n' "$TAB" "$TAB" >"$B/c-keep.listing"
    printf 'x.1.in.xlsx%s1\nx.1.out.xlsx%s1\ny.1.out.xlsx%s1\n' "$TAB" "$TAB" "$TAB" >"$B/c-keep-odd.listing"
    echo "  planted keep listing: pairs $(count_matches -E "[.]in[.]xlsx${TAB}" "$B/c-keep.listing"), files $(count_lines "$B/c-keep.listing"); with an unpaired output: pairs $(count_matches -E "[.]in[.]xlsx${TAB}" "$B/c-keep-odd.listing"), files $(count_lines "$B/c-keep-odd.listing")"
    check "keep_pairs_ok passes a planted listing of one whole pair" "$(yn keep_pairs_ok "$B/c-keep.listing")"
    check "control: keep_pairs_ok refuses a planted listing with an unpaired output" "$(ynnot keep_pairs_ok "$B/c-keep-odd.listing")"
    mkdir -p "$B/c-run/abc123" && printf 'a' >"$B/c-run/summary.host.tsv" && printf 'bb' >"$B/c-run/abc123/out.host.xlsx" && printf 'ccc' >"$B/c-run/abc123/stdout.host.txt"
    run_listing "$B/c-run" "$B/c-run.listing"
    echo "  planted run directory: files $(find "$B/c-run" -type f | wc -l); listing lines $(count_lines "$B/c-run.listing"); listing sha256 $(sha_of "$B/c-run.listing")"
    check "run_listing_ok passes the planted run directory's own listing" "$(yn run_listing_ok "$B/c-run" "$B/c-run.listing")"
    { cat "$B/c-run.listing"; head -n 1 "$B/c-run.listing"; } >"$B/c-run-dup.listing"
    check "control: run_listing_ok refuses a listing that names one file twice" "$(ynnot run_listing_ok "$B/c-run" "$B/c-run-dup.listing")"
    n_cargo=$(pgrep -x cargo | wc -l)
    n_rustc=$(pgrep -x rustc | wc -l)
    echo "SERIALIZED: no other log run was in flight; cargo processes at entry: $n_cargo; rustc processes at entry: $n_rustc; this run builds into <target>/main, the main tree's subdirectory of the phase's target root (CARGO_TARGET_DIR; change NSK)"
    no_build_running() { [ "$((n_cargo + n_rustc))" = 0 ]; }
    check "no cargo or rustc process was running at entry" "$(yn no_build_running)"
    echo "DETACHED: no interactive call waits on this run; stdout and stderr go to a file, polled from later calls."
    echo "TIMEOUT CHOSEN BEFORE THE RUN: --timeout 300 for the sample's child and --lo-timeout $LO_TIMEOUT_S per conversion, the figures every corpus run since Milestone 3 used; not tuned during the run."
    echo "root: <repo> stands for the repository's top level (inside <home>, scrubbed after <runs> and <corpus>, whose paths begin with it); scripts/counting.sh is read from it at the phase commit by git show; scripts/passthrough-run.sh, scripts/passthrough-record.py and scripts/edit-open-check.sh are run from it, each checked equal to the phase commit's, and the runner and the open check each source scripts/lo-check.sh, which is never run; the keep's tests run in it; the two record pairs are installed into its $RECORDS_DEST/"
    echo "root: <home> stands for the home directory of the account that ran this script"
    echo "root: <phase> stands for <home>/.cache/emend-build/m5p1-p1 on the disk, the phase's directory"
    echo "root: <scripts> stands for <phase>/scripts on the disk, this script's own directory, which holds the script and namedcmp.py beside it; the two record pairs are written into <scripts>/out/records first, a superseded run directory and a superseded keep are moved into <scripts>/out/superseded, and this script's own standard error goes to <scripts>/out/run.stderr (specs/0017 P1 verification ruling 7)"
    echo "root: <work> stands for this run's working directory, made by mktemp -d under <scripts>/out on the disk (the counting library, the comparison copied from beside this script, their outputs, derived tables, the planted listings and run directory, the runs' TMPDIR <work>/tmp-run, the open check's TMPDIR <work>/tmp), kept after the run and never removed"
    echo "root: <target> stands for <phase>/target on the disk, the phase's one target root: this log builds <repo> into <target>/main, the main tree's subdirectory, release binaries and the keep's tests, and into no other (change NSK)"
    echo "root: <keep> stands for <phase>/keep-host on the disk unless RUN_KEEP names another for a dry run, this phase's host keep; kept after the run for planning"
    echo "root: <corpus> stands for the private corpus directory (the manifest and the inputs under <corpus>/corpus, read)"
    echo "root: <runs> stands for the corpus run directories' parent, <corpus>/runs unless RUN_OUT_ROOT names another for a dry run; this log's run directory <runs>/$RUN-$SAMPLE is written there"
    apart() { case "$1/" in "$2"/*) return 1 ;; esac; case "$2/" in "$1"/*) return 1 ;; esac; return 0; }
    roots_distinct() {
      local a b all=("$SELF_DIR" "$BUILD_ROOT" "$MAIN" "$KEEP" "$CORPUS")
      for a in "${all[@]}"; do for b in "${all[@]}"; do
        [ "$a" = "$b" ] && continue
        apart "$a" "$b" || return 1
      done; done
    }
    check "the roots other than <home>, <phase>, <work> and <runs> are distinct, none inside another" "$(yn roots_distinct)"
    work_in_scripts() { case "$B/" in "$SELF_DIR/out/"*) return 0 ;; esac; return 1; }
    check "<work> is under <scripts>/out on the disk" "$(yn work_in_scripts)"
    work_ctl() { local B=/tmp/x; work_in_scripts; }
    check "control: the same test refuses a working directory under /tmp" "$(ynnot work_ctl)"
    runs_apart() { apart "$RUN_OUT_ROOT" "$MAIN" && apart "$RUN_OUT_ROOT" "$SELF_DIR"; }
    check "<runs> lies outside <repo> and <scripts>" "$(yn runs_apart)"
    check "control: apart refuses <target>/main/release against <target>/main, which holds it" "$(ynnot apart "$BUILD_ROOT/release" "$BUILD_ROOT")"
    echo "ANTHROPIC_API_KEY set in this shell: $([ -n "${ANTHROPIC_API_KEY:-}" ] && echo yes || echo no)"
    key_unset() { [ -z "${ANTHROPIC_API_KEY:-}" ]; }
    check "ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is not set" "$(yn key_unset)"
    key_set_ctl() { local ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=planted; key_unset; }
    check "control: the same check refuses a shell where the variable is set" "$(ynnot key_set_ctl)"
    echo "the run directories: <runs>/$RUN-$SAMPLE"
    echo "the record stems: $STEM and $STEM_OPEN; the records' destination: $RECORDS_DEST; RUN_SKIP_KEEP: $RUN_SKIP_KEEP"
    echo "at entry: status lines $entry_all; of them admitted by the phase's pattern (this phase's logs, its two record pairs, planning's modified specs/0032) $entry_ours; the lines:"
    git status --porcelain | sed 's/^/    /'
    ours_ctl() { printf ' M scripts/check.sh\n' | LC_ALL=C "$G" -qE "$OURS"; }
    check "control: the phase's status pattern refuses a modified gate file" "$(ynnot ours_ctl)"
    ours_rec_ctl() { printf '?? records/logs/m5p1-p1/run.log\n?? records/logs/m4p2-p2/run.log\n?? records/m5p1-p1-%s-%s.md\n?? records/m5p1-open-%s-%s.txt\n?? records/m5p1-p1-%s-abcdef0.md\n?? records/logs/m5p1-p1x/run.log\n M ROADMAP.md\n M specs/0032-read-breadth-styles.md\n M records/m5p1-p1-%s-%s.md\n M crates/emend/src/styles.rs\n' "$DATE" "$SHORT" "$DATE" "$SHORT" "$DATE" "$DATE" "$SHORT" | count_matches -E "$OURS" /dev/stdin; }
    check "control: the phase's status pattern admits this phase's log, its two untracked record pairs and planning's modified specs/0032 alone; it refuses another phase's log, a record of another commit, a sibling directory, ROADMAP.md, a modified record and a source file (change NSB)" "$(yn [ "$(ours_rec_ctl)" = 4 ])"
    echo
    echo "## script that wrote this log"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$SELF"
    echo
    echo "## the shared counting library this log sources (the phase commit's, by git show; change NSB)"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$B/counting.sh"
    echo
    echo "## counting controls"
    counting_controls
    if [ "$counting_controls_ok" != yes ]; then fail=1; fi
    
    echo
    echo "## the scripts, against the phase commit, and planning's uncommitted spec"
    tree_is_commit() { [ "$(sha_of "$1")" = "$(git show "$C:$1" | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1)" ]; }
    for s in scripts/passthrough-run.sh scripts/passthrough-record.py scripts/lo-check.sh scripts/edit-open-check.sh; do
      check "$s in the main tree is the phase commit's (sha256 $(sha_of "$s"))" "$(yn tree_is_commit "$s")"
    done
    tree_ctl() { [ "$(git show "$C:scripts/excel-check-list.py" | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1)" = "$(sha_of scripts/edit-open-check.sh)" ]; }
    check "control: the same hash comparison tells two different scripts apart" "$(ynnot tree_ctl)"
    spec_now=$(sha_of "$SPEC")
    spec_committed=$(git show "$C:$SPEC" | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1)
    spec_doc=$(git show "$DOC:$SPEC" | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1)
    echo "command: git show <phase commit>:$SPEC | sha256sum; git show <doc commit>:$SPEC | sha256sum; sha256sum $SPEC (the working file, printed and not asserted: planning holds its rulings during P1 uncommitted; change NSA)"
    echo "  at the phase commit: $spec_committed; at the doc commit: $spec_doc; the pin: $SPEC_WANT"
    echo "  the working tree's copy (planning's uncommitted rulings): sha256 $spec_now"
    spec_ok() { [ "$spec_committed" = "$SPEC_WANT" ]; }
    check "the spec at the phase commit is at the pinned hash" "$(yn spec_ok)"
    check "the spec at the phase commit is the doc commit's" "$(yn [ "$spec_committed" = "$spec_doc" ])"
    spec_ctl() { local spec_committed=1111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111; spec_ok; }
    check "control: the same check refuses the spec against another hash" "$(ynnot spec_ctl)"
    echo "command: podman image exists $IMAGE"
    check "the pinned LibreOffice image is there" "$(yn podman image exists "$IMAGE")"
    
    echo
    echo "## the release binaries, built here at the phase commit, both targets"
    echo "command: cargo build --release -p emend-copy -p xlsx-diff; the same with --target $I686 (CARGO_TARGET_DIR=<target>/main)"
    cargo build --release -p emend-copy -p xlsx-diff >"$B/build-host.out" 2>&1 </dev/null
    rc_h=$?
    cargo build --release -p emend-copy -p xlsx-diff --target "$I686" >"$B/build-i686.out" 2>&1 </dev/null
    rc_i=$?
    echo "  exit: host $rc_h, $I686 $rc_i"
    check "both release builds exit 0" "$(yn [ "$((rc_h + rc_i))" = 0 ])"
    PT_host=$CARGO_TARGET_DIR/release/emend-copy
    XD_host=$CARGO_TARGET_DIR/release/xlsx-diff
    PT_i686=$CARGO_TARGET_DIR/$I686/release/emend-copy
    XD_i686=$CARGO_TARGET_DIR/$I686/release/xlsx-diff
    for b in "$PT_host" "$XD_host" "$PT_i686" "$XD_i686"; do echo "  $b: sha256 $(sha_of "$b"), bytes $(stat -c %s "$b")"; done
    echo "  $(rustc --version)"
    
    echo
    echo "## the corpus manifest, and its workbooks holding a calculation chain (specs/0025 P3 verification ruling 4; change NSI)"
    awk -F'\t' 'NR == 1 { for (i = 1; i <= NF; i++) k[$i] = i; next } { print $k["id"] "\t" $k["ext"] }' "$CORPUS/manifest.tsv" >"$B/order"
    manifest_rows=$(count_lines "$B/order")
    n_regular=$(find "$CORPUS/corpus" -maxdepth 1 -type f | wc -l)
    echo "command: awk over <corpus>/manifest.tsv's id and ext columns by header name; find <corpus>/corpus -maxdepth 1 -type f"
    echo "  manifest rows: $manifest_rows; regular files under <corpus>/corpus: $n_regular"
    check "the manifest names one workbook per regular file of the corpus directory" "$(yn [ "$manifest_rows" = "$n_regular" ])"
    check "the manifest names some workbook" "$(yn [ "$manifest_rows" -ge 1 ])"
    : >"$B/chain-ids"
    while IFS="$TAB" read -r id ext; do
      if [ "$(python3 -c 'import sys, zipfile; print(1 if "xl/calcChain.xml" in zipfile.ZipFile(sys.argv[1]).namelist() else 0)' "$CORPUS/corpus/$id.$ext")" = 1 ]; then
        printf '%s\n' "$id" >>"$B/chain-ids"
      fi
    done <"$B/order"
    N_CHAIN=$(count_lines "$B/chain-ids")
    echo "command: python3 -c <zipfile namelist> <corpus>/corpus/<id>.<ext>, for each manifest row"
    echo "  corpus workbooks holding xl/calcChain.xml: $N_CHAIN of $manifest_rows (ids: $(paste -sd' ' "$B/chain-ids"))"
    echo "  the rule covering them (change NSI): the sample writes no cell, so each calcChain entry is identical and unflagged on both labels, and none is dropped"
    check "some corpus workbook holds a calculation chain, so the chain rows below are read" "$(yn [ "$N_CHAIN" -ge 1 ])"
    
    echo
    echo "## the run log's comparison (python3, zipfile, byte spans and ElementTree; change NSC)"
    cp "$SELF_DIR/namedcmp.py" "$B/namedcmp.py" || exit 2
    echo "command: cp <scripts>/namedcmp.py <work>/namedcmp.py; sed 's/^/    /' <work>/namedcmp.py; sha256 $(sha_of "$B/namedcmp.py"), $(wc -c <"$B/namedcmp.py") bytes"
    check "the copy is the file beside this script, byte for byte" "$(yn cmp -s "$SELF_DIR/namedcmp.py" "$B/namedcmp.py")"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$B/namedcmp.py"
    FLAGS="rest_same dxfs_prefix appended_match entries_same xml_values flagged"
    # flags_of_cmp <comparison> <mode>: its FLAGS_OF entry, read from its source
    # with ast.
    flags_of_cmp() {
      python3 -c 'import ast, sys
    tree = ast.parse(open(sys.argv[1]).read())
    for node in tree.body:
        if isinstance(node, ast.Assign) and getattr(node.targets[0], "id", "") == "FLAGS_OF":
            print(" ".join(ast.literal_eval(node.value)[sys.argv[2]]))' "$1" "$2"
    }
    echo "  namedstyles: the comparison's FLAGS_OF, read from its source: $(flags_of_cmp "$B/namedcmp.py" namedstyles)"
    check "this log's flag list is the comparison's" "$(yn [ "$(flags_of_cmp "$B/namedcmp.py" namedstyles)" = "$FLAGS" ])"
    printf 'FLAGS_OF = {"namedstyles": ("rest_same",)}\n' >"$B/c-flags.py"
    check "control: the same reader gives another list for a planted source" "$(yn [ "$(flags_of_cmp "$B/c-flags.py" namedstyles)" = rest_same ])"
    kv() { printf '%s\n' "$1" | tr '\t ' '\n\n' | sed -n "s/^$2=//p" | head -1; }
    # all_yes <comparison line>: every flag yes.
    all_yes() { local f; for f in $FLAGS; do [ "$(kv "$1" "$f")" = yes ] || return 1; done; }
    # The tool's keys, in its order (tools/emend-copy, --namedstyles-sample);
    # the comparison prints the same keys (change NSC).
    KEYS="named named_xfs builtin custom resolved default_font_size dxfs dxf_fonts dxf_fills dxf_borders dxf_numfmts dxf_alignments dxf_protections dxf_gradients dxf_implied_solid dxf_inside_sides dxf_written dxf_equal"
    # tool_and_cmp <tool line> <comparison line>: every key the same.
    tool_and_cmp() {
      local k
      for k in $KEYS; do
        [ -n "$(kv "$2" "$k")" ] || return 1
        [ "$(kv "$1" "$k")" = "$(kv "$2" "$k")" ] || return 1
      done
    }
    # line_as_spec <tool line>: what "Harness runs" expects of the line: the
    # word namedstyles and the keys in the tool's order, each a number (the
    # default font's size a decimal); resolved equal to named_xfs and dxf_equal
    # to dxf_written, both asserted by the tool; every dxf count within dxfs,
    # builtin and custom within named, the implied solid fills within the fills.
    line_as_spec() {
      local n got
      [ "$(printf '%s' "$1" | cut -f1)" = namedstyles ] || return 1
      got=$(printf '%s' "$1" | cut -f2- | tr '\t' '\n' | sed 's/=.*//' | tr '\n' ' ')
      [ "$got" = "$KEYS " ] || return 1
      for n in $KEYS; do
        case "$n" in
          default_font_size) printf '%s' "$(kv "$1" "$n")" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -qxE '[0-9]+([.][0-9]+)?' || return 1 ;;
          *) case "$(kv "$1" "$n")" in '' | *[!0-9]*) return 1 ;; esac ;;
        esac
      done
      [ "$(kv "$1" resolved)" = "$(kv "$1" named_xfs)" ] || return 1
      [ "$(kv "$1" dxf_equal)" = "$(kv "$1" dxf_written)" ] || return 1
      for n in dxf_fonts dxf_fills dxf_borders dxf_numfmts dxf_alignments dxf_protections dxf_gradients dxf_implied_solid dxf_inside_sides dxf_written; do
        [ "$n" = dxf_inside_sides ] && continue
        [ "$(kv "$1" "$n")" -le "$(kv "$1" dxfs)" ] || return 1
      done
      [ "$(kv "$1" builtin)" -le "$(kv "$1" named)" ] && [ "$(kv "$1" custom)" -le "$(kv "$1" named)" ] \
        && [ "$(kv "$1" dxf_implied_solid)" -le "$(kv "$1" dxf_fills)" ]
    }
    check "control: all_yes refuses a line with no flags" "$(ynnot all_yes "found=1")"
    LINE_C=$(printf 'namedstyles\tnamed=7\tnamed_xfs=21\tbuiltin=6\tcustom=0\tresolved=21\tdefault_font_size=10.5\tdxfs=5\tdxf_fonts=1\tdxf_fills=5\tdxf_borders=0\tdxf_numfmts=0\tdxf_alignments=0\tdxf_protections=0\tdxf_gradients=0\tdxf_implied_solid=1\tdxf_inside_sides=2\tdxf_written=5\tdxf_equal=5')
    check "control: line_as_spec accepts a line as the spec reads" "$(yn line_as_spec "$LINE_C")"
    for bad in "s/resolved=21/resolved=20/" "s/dxf_equal=5/dxf_equal=4/" "s/dxf_fonts=1/dxf_fonts=6/" "s/custom=0/custom=8/" \
               "s/default_font_size=10.5/default_font_size=x/" "s/dxf_implied_solid=1/dxf_implied_solid=6/" "s/\tdxf_gradients=0//" "s/^namedstyles/roundtrip/"; do
      lin_ctl() { line_as_spec "$(printf '%s' "$LINE_C" | sed "$bad")"; }
      check "control: line_as_spec refuses the line changed by $bad" "$(ynnot lin_ctl)"
    done
    CMP_C=$(printf '%s' "$LINE_C" | cut -f2- | tr '\t' ' ')
    check "control: tool_and_cmp accepts a pair that agrees" "$(yn tool_and_cmp "$LINE_C" "$CMP_C")"
    tac_ctl() { tool_and_cmp "$LINE_C" "$(printf '%s' "$CMP_C" | sed 's/dxf_inside_sides=2/dxf_inside_sides=1/')"; }
    check "control: tool_and_cmp refuses a pair whose inside sides disagree" "$(ynnot tac_ctl)"
    tac_ctl2() { tool_and_cmp "$LINE_C" "$(printf '%s' "$CMP_C" | sed 's/default_font_size=10.5/default_font_size=10/')"; }
    check "control: tool_and_cmp refuses a pair whose default font sizes disagree" "$(ynnot tac_ctl2)"
    tac_ctl3() { tool_and_cmp "$LINE_C" "$(printf '%s' "$CMP_C" | sed 's/ dxf_written=5//')"; }
    check "control: tool_and_cmp refuses a comparison line missing a key" "$(ynnot tac_ctl3)"
    
    count_where() { awk -F'\t' -v c="$2" -v v="$3" 'NR == 1 { for (i = 1; i <= NF; i++) if ($i == c) k = i; next } k && $k == v { n++ } END { print n + 0 }' "$1"; }
    # count_ok_where <summary> <column> <value>: among the rows whose outcome is ok.
    count_ok_where() { awk -F'\t' -v c="$2" -v v="$3" 'NR == 1 { for (i = 1; i <= NF; i++) { if ($i == c) k = i; if ($i == "outcome") o = i }; next } k && o && $o == "ok" && $k == v { n++ } END { print n + 0 }' "$1"; }
    sum_col() { awk -F'\t' -v c="$2" 'NR == 1 { for (i = 1; i <= NF; i++) if ($i == c) k = i; next } k { n += $k } END { print n + 0 }' "$1"; }
    # status_rows <entries> <status>: the entry rows of that status, every
    # workbook.
    status_rows() { awk -F'\t' -v s="$2" 'NR == 1 { for (i = 1; i <= NF; i++) if ($i == "status") k = i; next } k && $k == s { n++ } END { print n + 0 }' "$1"; }
    # The styles part and the dxfs the sample writes back, for each workbook,
    # read once from the input by the comparison and never printed.
    while IFS="$TAB" read -r id ext; do
      python3 "$B/namedcmp.py" namedstyles "$CORPUS/corpus/$id.$ext" --parts >"$B/parts-$id"
    done <"$B/order"
    n_pc=0; n_written=0
    while IFS="$TAB" read -r id ext; do
      if [ "$(count_lines "$B/parts-$id")" = 2 ] && sed -n 2p "$B/parts-$id" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -qxE '[0-9]+'; then
        n_pc=$((n_pc + 1))
        if [ "$(sed -n 2p "$B/parts-$id")" -gt 0 ]; then n_written=$((n_written + 1)); fi
      fi
    done <"$B/order"
    echo "  inputs whose styles part the comparison found, with its count of dxfs the sample writes back (two lines): $n_pc of $manifest_rows; of them with some dxf written back: $n_written"
    check "the comparison found the styles part in every input" "$(yn [ "$n_pc" = "$manifest_rows" ])"
    both_written_cases() { [ "$n_written" -ge 1 ] && [ "$n_written" -lt "$n_pc" ]; }
    check "some input has a dxf the sample writes back and some none, so both cases of the entries rule and of the plants are read" "$(yn both_written_cases)"
    # entries_named <entries> <id> <parts file>: the runner's rows for one
    # workbook as "Harness runs" gives them (change NSE): the styles part
    # changed, flagged descriptor at most, exactly when the sample writes some
    # dxf back (parts line 2 above 0), else identical and unflagged; every other
    # row identical and unflagged; nothing added, dropped or recompressed.
    entries_named() {
      local sp w
      sp=$(sed -n 1p "$3"); w=$(sed -n 2p "$3")
      [ -n "$sp" ] && [ -n "$w" ] || return 1
      awk -F'\t' -v id="$2" -v sp="$sp" -v w="$w" '
        NR == 1 { for (c = 1; c <= NF; c++) k[$c] = c; next }
        $k["id"] != id { next }
        {
          n++
          nm = $k["name"]; st = $k["status"]; fl = $k["flags"]
          if (nm == sp) {
            seen = 1
            want = (w > 0) ? "changed" : "identical"
            if (st != want) bad++
            if (st == "changed") { if (fl != "" && fl != "descriptor") bad++ }
            else if (fl != "") bad++
          } else if (st != "identical" || fl != "") bad++
        }
        END { if (n == 0 || !seen || bad > 0) exit 1 }' "$1"
    }
    # chain_rows_of <entries> <id>: the workbook's calcChain rows, those
    # identical and unflagged, and those dropped (change NSI).
    chain_rows_of() {
      awk -F'\t' -v id="$2" '
        NR == 1 { for (i = 1; i <= NF; i++) col[$i] = i; next }
        $col["id"] == id && $col["name"] == "xl/calcChain.xml" { n++; if ($col["status"] == "identical" && $col["flags"] == "") s++; if ($col["status"] == "dropped") d++ }
        END { print n + 0, s + 0, d + 0 }' "$1"
    }
    # The rule's controls: each allowance accepted where it applies and refused
    # on a planted row where it does not (change NSE).
    printf 'xl/styles.xml\n2\n' >"$B/pc-changed"
    printf 'xl/styles.xml\n0\n' >"$B/pc-kept"
    etsv() { { printf 'id\tname\tstatus\tflags\n'; printf "$@"; } >"$B/ce.tsv"; }
    en_yes() { entries_named "$B/ce.tsv" w "$1"; }
    etsv 'w\txl/styles.xml\tchanged\tdescriptor\nw\t[Content_Types].xml\tidentical\t\nw\txl/workbook.xml\tidentical\t\n'
    check "control: entries_named accepts the styles part changed, flagged descriptor, where a dxf is written back" "$(yn en_yes "$B/pc-changed")"
    check "control: entries_named refuses the same rows where nothing is written back" "$(ynnot en_yes "$B/pc-kept")"
    etsv 'w\txl/styles.xml\tidentical\t\nw\t[Content_Types].xml\tidentical\t\nw\txl/workbook.xml\tidentical\t\n'
    check "control: entries_named accepts every row identical where nothing is written back" "$(yn en_yes "$B/pc-kept")"
    check "control: entries_named refuses the styles part identical where a dxf is written back" "$(ynnot en_yes "$B/pc-changed")"
    etsv 'w\txl/styles.xml\tchanged\t\nw\t[Content_Types].xml\tchanged\t\nw\txl/workbook.xml\tidentical\t\n'
    check "control: entries_named refuses another changed row" "$(ynnot en_yes "$B/pc-changed")"
    etsv 'w\txl/styles.xml\tchanged\t\nw\txl/calcChain.xml\trecompressed\t\n'
    check "control: entries_named refuses a recompressed row" "$(ynnot en_yes "$B/pc-changed")"
    etsv 'w\txl/styles.xml\tchanged\tgpflags\nw\txl/workbook.xml\tidentical\t\n'
    check "control: entries_named refuses the styles part flagged other than descriptor" "$(ynnot en_yes "$B/pc-changed")"
    etsv 'w\txl/styles.xml\tidentical\tdescriptor\nw\txl/workbook.xml\tidentical\t\n'
    check "control: entries_named refuses an identical row flagged" "$(ynnot en_yes "$B/pc-kept")"
    etsv 'w\txl/styles.xml\tchanged\t\nw\txl/planted.xml\tadded\t\n'
    check "control: entries_named refuses an added row" "$(ynnot en_yes "$B/pc-changed")"
    etsv 'w\txl/styles.xml\tchanged\t\nw\txl/calcChain.xml\tdropped\t\n'
    check "control: entries_named refuses a dropped row" "$(ynnot en_yes "$B/pc-changed")"
    etsv 'w\txl/workbook.xml\tidentical\t\n'
    check "control: entries_named refuses the rows with no styles part" "$(ynnot en_yes "$B/pc-kept")"
    etsv 'w\txl/styles.xml\tidentical\t\nw\txl/calcChain.xml\tidentical\t\n'
    check "control: chain_rows_of reads the planted workbook's one calcChain row, identical and unflagged" "$(yn [ "$(chain_rows_of "$B/ce.tsv" w)" = "1 1 0" ])"
    etsv 'w\txl/styles.xml\tidentical\t\nw\txl/calcChain.xml\tdropped\t\n'
    check "control: chain_rows_of reads a dropped calcChain row as dropped" "$(yn [ "$(chain_rows_of "$B/ce.tsv" w)" = "1 0 1" ])"
    # refusal_of <run dir> <id> <label>: the layer's one "error: " line when the
    # row is a refusal, else nothing.
    refusal_of() { sed -n '1s/^error: //p' "$1/$2/stderr.$3.txt"; }
    
    echo
    echo "## TMPDIR for the corpus runs, on the disk"
    RUNTMP=$B/tmp-run
    mkdir "$RUNTMP" || exit 2
    dev_tmp=$(stat -c %d "$RUNTMP")
    dev_corpus=$(stat -c %d "$CORPUS/corpus")
    dev_proc=$(stat -c %d /proc)
    echo "command: mkdir <work>/tmp-run; stat -c %d <work>/tmp-run <corpus>/corpus /proc; df --output=fstype,target <work>/tmp-run <corpus>/corpus"
    echo "  device of TMPDIR (<work>/tmp-run): $dev_tmp; of the corpus directory (<corpus>/corpus): $dev_corpus; of /proc (the control): $dev_proc"
    df --output=fstype,target "$RUNTMP" "$CORPUS/corpus" | sed 's/^/    /'
    check "TMPDIR for the corpus runs and the corpus directory are on one device" "$(yn [ "$dev_tmp" = "$dev_corpus" ])"
    check "control: the same comparison tells /proc's device from the corpus directory's" "$(yn [ "$dev_proc" != "$dev_corpus" ])"
    
    cat >"$B/reccheck.py" <<'PY'
    """This log's check of a passthrough record against its run directory, for
    every label the directory holds. Reads the record's .txt and .md and the run
    directory's summary.<label>.tsv, entries.<label>.tsv and each workbook's
    diff.<label>.tsv; prints one "name: yes|no" line per check and one line of
    counts. It imports only the part-family rules from
    scripts/passthrough-record.py, so the check covers the record's tables and
    its counting, not the family names. Change VJ: the dropped families are an
    input, as the changed and added ones are."""
    import importlib.util
    import os
    import sys
    
    sys.dont_write_bytecode = True
    rec_script, run_dir, txt, md, want_changed, want_added, want_dropped, tool_arg = sys.argv[1:9]
    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location("record", rec_script)
    record = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)
    spec.loader.exec_module(record)
    
    
    def lines(path):
        out = open(path, encoding="utf-8").read().split("\n")
        return out[:-1] if out and out[-1] == "" else out
    
    
    def listed(value):
        return value.split(",") if value else []
    
    
    labels = [l for l in ("host", "i686") if os.path.exists("%s/summary.%s.tsv" % (run_dir, l))]
    tables = "\n".join(lines(txt)).split("\n\n")
    summary, entries, xml = [], [], ["\t".join(record.XML_HEADER)]
    per_label = {}
    for label in labels:
        s = lines("%s/summary.%s.tsv" % (run_dir, label))
        e = lines("%s/entries.%s.tsv" % (run_dir, label))
        summary = summary or [s[0]]
        entries = entries or [e[0]]
        summary += s[1:]
        entries += e[1:]
        x = []
        for row in s[1:]:
            cells = dict(zip(s[0].split("\t"), row.split("\t")))
            if cells["outcome"] != "ok" or cells["diff_exit"] not in ("0", "1"):
                continue
            for line in lines("%s/%s/diff.%s.tsv" % (run_dir, cells["id"], label)):
                c = line.split("\t")
                if c[0] == "xml":
                    x.append("\t".join([cells["id"], label] + c + [""] * (10 - 2 - len(c))))
        xml += x
        per_label[label] = (e, x)
    checks = [
        ("three tables", len(tables) == 3),
        ("the summary table is every label's summary", len(tables) == 3 and tables[0].split("\n") == summary),
        ("the entries table is every label's entries", len(tables) == 3 and tables[1].split("\n") == entries),
        ("the xml table is every compared workbook's xml rows", len(tables) == 3 and tables[2].split("\n") == xml),
    ]
    text = lines(md)
    
    
    def section(title):
        out, on = [], False
        for line in text:
            if line == "## " + title:
                on = True
                continue
            if on and line.startswith("## "):
                break
            if on and line.startswith("| ") and not line.startswith("| ---"):
                out.append(line)
        return out[1:]
    
    
    def row(cells):
        return "| " + " | ".join(str(c) for c in cells) + " |"
    
    
    cols = ("entries",) + record.STATUSES + ("flagged",) + record.FLAGS
    xcols = ("compared", "parse_errors", "names_equal", "values_equal", "in_only", "out_only")
    for label in labels:
        e, x = per_label[label]
        head = e[0].split("\t")
        fam = {}
        for line in e[1:]:
            r = dict(zip(head, line.split("\t")))
            c = fam.setdefault(record.family(r["name"]), dict.fromkeys(cols, 0))
            c["entries"] += 1
            c[r["status"]] = c.get(r["status"], 0) + 1
            flags = [f for f in r["flags"].split(",") if f]
            c["flagged"] += 1 if flags else 0
            for f in flags:
                c[f] = c.get(f, 0) + 1
        want = [row([f] + [fam[f][k] for k in cols]) for f in record.FAMILIES if f in fam]
        want.append(row(["total"] + [sum(fam[f][k] for f in fam) for k in cols]))
        checks.append(("%s: each family row of Entries by part family" % label, section("Entries by part family: " + label) == want))
        xf, cur = {}, None
        for line in x:
            c = line.split("\t")
            name, kind = c[3], c[4]
            if kind == "parse":
                cur = xf.setdefault(record.family(name), dict.fromkeys(xcols, 0))
                cur["compared"] += 1
                parsed = c[5] == "ok" and c[6] == "ok"
                cur["parse_errors"] += 0 if parsed else 1
                differ = False
            elif kind in ("element", "attribute"):
                differ = True
            elif kind == "values":
                cur["names_equal"] += 1 if parsed and not differ else 0
                cur["values_equal"] += 1 if c[7] == "0" and c[8] == "0" else 0
                cur["in_only"] += int(c[7])
                cur["out_only"] += int(c[8])
        want = [row([f] + [xf[f][k] for k in xcols]) for f in record.FAMILIES if f in xf]
        want.append(row(["total"] + [sum(xf[f][k] for f in xf) for k in xcols]))
        checks.append(("%s: each family row of the XML comparison" % label, section("XML comparison of changed entries: " + label) == want))
        changed_f = sorted(f for f in fam if fam[f].get("changed"))
        dropped_f = sorted(f for f in fam if fam[f].get("dropped"))
        added_f = sorted(f for f in fam if fam[f].get("added"))
        checks.append(("%s: the xml families are the changed entries' families" % label, sorted(xf) == changed_f))
        checks.append(("%s: the changed entries' families are %s" % (label, want_changed or "none"), changed_f == listed(want_changed)))
        checks.append(("%s: the dropped entries' families are %s" % (label, want_dropped or "none"), dropped_f == listed(want_dropped)))
        checks.append(("%s: the added entries' families are %s" % (label, want_added or "none"), added_f == listed(want_added)))
    checks.append(("the record's Targets line", "- Targets: " + ", ".join(labels) in text))
    checks.append(("the record's Tool arguments line", "- Tool arguments: " + tool_arg in text))
    for name, ok in checks:
        print("%s: %s" % (name, "yes" if ok else "no"))
    print("labels %s; summary rows %d; entry rows %d; xml rows %d" % (",".join(labels), len(summary) - 1, len(entries) - 1, len(xml) - 1))
    PY
    fams_of() {
      python3 -c 'import importlib.util, sys
    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location("record", sys.argv[1])
    record = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)
    spec.loader.exec_module(record)
    rows = [l.split("\t", 1) for l in open(sys.argv[2]).read().split("\n") if l]
    print(",".join(sorted({record.family(n) for (k, n) in rows if k == sys.argv[3]})))' scripts/passthrough-record.py "$1" "$2"
    }
    inst_same() { cmp -s "$RECORDS/$1" "$RECORDS_DEST/$1" && [ "$(stat -c %a "$RECORDS_DEST/$1")" = 644 ]; }
    # Change JI: no bytecode was written, so there is nothing to remove.
    no_pycache() { [ ! -e scripts/__pycache__ ]; }
    for label in host i686; do
      var=PT_$label; PT=${!var}; var=XD_$label; XD=${!var}
      echo
      echo "## $SAMPLE: $label run, --tool-arg $EDIT"
      echo "command: TMPDIR=<work>/tmp-run scripts/passthrough-run.sh --label $label --passthrough <target>/main/$([ "$label" = i686 ] && echo "$I686/")release/emend-copy --xlsx-diff <target>/main/$([ "$label" = i686 ] && echo "$I686/")release/xlsx-diff --out <runs>/$RUN-$SAMPLE --libreoffice $IMAGE --lo-timeout $LO_TIMEOUT_S --timeout 300 --tool-arg $EDIT"
      started=$(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)
      TMPDIR=$RUNTMP scripts/passthrough-run.sh --label "$label" --passthrough "$PT" --xlsx-diff "$XD" --out "$O" \
        --libreoffice "$IMAGE" --lo-timeout "$LO_TIMEOUT_S" --timeout 300 --tool-arg "$EDIT" \
        >"$B/run-$label.stdout" 2>"$B/run-$label.stderr" </dev/null
      rc=$?
      echo "  started $started; ended $(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ); exit $rc; stderr bytes: $(wc -c <"$B/run-$label.stderr")"
      sed 's/^/    /' "$B/run-$label.stdout"
      check "$label: the run exits 0" "$(yn [ "$rc" = 0 ])"
      check "$label: its stderr is empty" "$(yn [ ! -s "$B/run-$label.stderr" ])"
      n_left=$(find "$RUNTMP" -mindepth 1 | wc -l)
      echo "  entries left in <work>/tmp-run after the run: $n_left"
      check "$label: the runs' TMPDIR is empty after the run" "$(yn [ "$n_left" = 0 ])"
      SUM=$O/summary.$label.tsv
      ENT=$O/entries.$label.tsv
      rows=$(awk 'NR > 1' "$SUM" | wc -l)
      n_ok=$(count_where "$SUM" outcome ok)
      # The refusals, by id and message.
      : >"$B/refused-$label"
      while IFS="$TAB" read -r id ext; do
        if [ "$(awk -F'\t' -v id="$id" 'NR == 1 { for (i = 1; i <= NF; i++) k[$i] = i; next } $k["id"] == id { print $k["outcome"] " " $k["exit"] }' "$SUM")" = "error 2" ] \
           && [ "$(count_lines "$O/$id/stderr.$label.txt")" = 1 ] && [ -n "$(refusal_of "$O" "$id" "$label")" ]; then
          printf '%s\t%s\n' "$id" "$(refusal_of "$O" "$id" "$label")" >>"$B/refused-$label"
        fi
      done <"$B/order"
      n_ref=$(count_lines "$B/refused-$label")
      echo "  summary rows: $rows; outcome ok: $n_ok; refused by the layer (a finding; fails the summary): $n_ref"
      sed 's/^/    refused: /' "$B/refused-$label"
      echo "  among the ok rows: lo ok $(count_ok_where "$SUM" lo ok); lo_in ok $(count_ok_where "$SUM" lo_in ok); leftover no $(count_ok_where "$SUM" leftover no); order_preserved yes $(count_ok_where "$SUM" order_preserved yes); comment_equal yes $(count_ok_where "$SUM" comment_equal yes); files_identical yes $(count_ok_where "$SUM" files_identical yes), no $(count_ok_where "$SUM" files_identical no) (printed, not asserted; change NSE)"
      echo "  every row: lo_in ok $(count_where "$SUM" lo_in ok); leftover no $(count_where "$SUM" leftover no)"
      echo "  entry totals: identical $(sum_col "$SUM" identical), recompressed $(sum_col "$SUM" recompressed), changed $(sum_col "$SUM" changed), dropped $(sum_col "$SUM" dropped), added $(sum_col "$SUM" added), flagged $(sum_col "$SUM" flagged)"
      echo "  the entries table's rows by status: identical $(status_rows "$ENT" identical), recompressed $(status_rows "$ENT" recompressed), changed $(status_rows "$ENT" changed), dropped $(status_rows "$ENT" dropped), added $(status_rows "$ENT" added)"
      # The totals the ok rows imply by the rule (change NSE).
      want_changed=0
      while IFS="$TAB" read -r id ext; do
        if [ -n "$(awk -F'\t' -v id="$id" '$1 == id' "$B/refused-$label")" ]; then continue; fi
        if [ "$(sed -n 2p "$B/parts-$id")" -gt 0 ]; then want_changed=$((want_changed + 1)); fi
      done <"$B/order"
      echo "  the entry totals the ok rows imply: changed $want_changed, added 0, dropped 0, none recompressed"
      summary_ok() {
        local col st
        [ "$rows" = "$manifest_rows" ] || return 1
        [ "$n_ok" = "$rows" ] && [ "$n_ref" = 0 ] || return 1
        for col in "lo ok" "lo_in ok" "leftover no" "order_preserved yes" "comment_equal yes"; do
          [ "$(count_ok_where "$SUM" ${col% *} ${col#* })" = "$n_ok" ] || return 1
        done
        [ "$(count_where "$SUM" lo_in ok)" = "$rows" ] || return 1
        [ "$(count_where "$SUM" leftover no)" = "$rows" ] || return 1
        [ "$(sum_col "$SUM" changed)" = "$want_changed" ] || return 1
        [ "$(sum_col "$SUM" added)" = 0 ] || return 1
        [ "$(sum_col "$SUM" dropped)" = 0 ] || return 1
        [ "$(sum_col "$SUM" recompressed)" = 0 ] || return 1
        for st in identical recompressed changed dropped added; do
          [ "$(sum_col "$SUM" "$st")" = "$(status_rows "$ENT" "$st")" ] || return 1
        done
      }
      check "$label: every row ok; every row's input opens (lo_in ok) with no leftover; every output opens (lo ok), order and comment kept; the changed total as the ok rows imply ($want_changed), none added, dropped or recompressed; the summary's status totals the entries table's" "$(yn summary_ok)"
      echo "  per ok workbook: id, the tool's line, the comparison's line (counts and yes/no only)"
      : >"$B/lines-$label"
      : >"$B/case-$label"
      nwb=0; nflags=0; nagree=0; nline=0; nentries=0; io=0; io_want=0; oo=0; oo_want=0; fl=0; fl_want=0
      nchain=0; nchain_same=0; nchain_drop=0
      while IFS="$TAB" read -r id ext; do
        if [ -n "$(awk -F'\t' -v id="$id" '$1 == id' "$B/refused-$label")" ]; then continue; fi
        nwb=$((nwb + 1))
        e=$(cat "$O/$id/stdout.$label.txt")
        c=$(python3 "$B/namedcmp.py" namedstyles "$CORPUS/corpus/$id.$ext" "$O/$id/out.$label.$ext" --diff "$O/$id/diff.$label.tsv")
        printf '%s\t%s\n' "$id" "$e" >>"$B/lines-$label"
        printf '    %s %s\n' "$id" "$(printf '%s' "$e" | tr '\t' ' ')"
        printf '    %s cmp %s\n' "$id" "$(printf '%s' "$c" | tr '\t' ' ')"
        # Change NSH: the case each workbook gives the plants.
        if [ "$(sed -n 2p "$B/parts-$id")" -gt 0 ]; then cs=changed; else cs=kept; fi
        printf '%s\t%s\n' "$id" "$cs" >>"$B/case-$label"
        if LC_ALL=C "$G" -qxF "$id" "$B/chain-ids"; then
          cr=$(chain_rows_of "$ENT" "$id")
          set -- $cr
          nchain=$((nchain + $1)); nchain_same=$((nchain_same + $2)); nchain_drop=$((nchain_drop + $3))
        fi
        io=$((io + $(kv "$c" in_only))); io_want=$((io_want + $(kv "$c" in_only_want)))
        oo=$((oo + $(kv "$c" out_only))); oo_want=$((oo_want + $(kv "$c" out_only_want)))
        fl=$((fl + $(kv "$c" flagged_rows))); fl_want=$((fl_want + $(kv "$c" flagged_want)))
        if all_yes "$c"; then nflags=$((nflags + 1)); else echo "    $id: a flag of the comparison does not hold"; fi
        if tool_and_cmp "$e" "$c"; then nagree=$((nagree + 1)); else echo "    $id: the tool and the comparison disagree"; fi
        if line_as_spec "$e"; then nline=$((nline + 1)); else echo "    $id: the tool's line is not what the spec reads"; fi
        if entries_named "$ENT" "$id" "$B/parts-$id"; then nentries=$((nentries + 1)); else echo "    $id: the entry rows are not what the rule gives"; fi
      done <"$B/order"
      echo "  ok workbooks read: $nwb; every flag holds: $nflags; the tool and the comparison agree: $nagree; the line as the spec reads: $nline; entry rows as the rule gives: $nentries"
      echo "  the plant cases over the ok workbooks (change NSH):"
      cut -f2 "$B/case-$label" | sed 's/^/case=/' | LC_ALL=C sort | uniq -c | sed 's/^/    /'
      echo "  the xml values rows over the ok workbooks: in_only $io, out_only $oo; the one-sided values the outputs give, counted by the comparison: $io_want and $oo_want"
      echo "  the flagged entry rows over the ok workbooks: $fl; rewritten entries whose descriptor bytes or bit 3 differ, counted by the comparison: $fl_want"
      check "$label: the comparison read every ok workbook" "$(yn [ "$nwb" = "$n_ok" ])"
      check "$label: every flag of the comparison holds in every ok workbook" "$(yn [ "$nflags" = "$n_ok" ])"
      check "$label: the tool's counts are the comparison's own counts of the input in every ok workbook (ruling 2's dxf_implied_solid and dxf_inside_sides among them)" "$(yn [ "$nagree" = "$n_ok" ])"
      check "$label: every line is what the spec reads" "$(yn [ "$nline" = "$n_ok" ])"
      check "$label: every ok workbook's entry rows are as the rule gives (change NSE)" "$(yn [ "$nentries" = "$n_ok" ])"
      vals_ok() { [ "$io" = "$io_want" ] && [ "$oo" = "$oo_want" ] && [ "$oo" -ge 1 ]; }
      check "$label: the in_only and out_only totals are the derived totals, and some value was written" "$(yn vals_ok)"
      fl_ok() { [ "$fl" = "$fl_want" ] && [ "$fl" = "$(sum_col "$SUM" flagged)" ]; }
      check "$label: the flagged total is the derived total and the summary's" "$(yn fl_ok)"
      echo "  calcChain rows in the ok rows of the chain workbooks: $nchain; identical and unflagged: $nchain_same; dropped: $nchain_drop (change NSI)"
      chain_kept() { [ "$nchain" = "$N_CHAIN" ] && [ "$nchain_same" = "$nchain" ] && [ "$nchain_drop" = 0 ]; }
      check "$label: every chain workbook has one calcChain row, identical and unflagged, none dropped (change NSI)" "$(yn chain_kept)"
      R=$O/run.$label.tsv
      args=$(awk -F'\t' 'NR == 1 { for (i = 1; i <= NF; i++) if ($i == "tool_args") k = i; next } k && NR == 2 { print $k }' "$R")
      bins_in_row() { [ "$(awk -F'\t' 'NR == 1 { for (i = 1; i <= NF; i++) k[$i] = i; next } NR == 2 { print $k["passthrough_sha256"] " " $k["xlsx_diff_sha256"] " " $k["commit"] }' "$R")" = "$(sha_of "$PT") $(sha_of "$XD") $C" ]; }
      check "$label: the run row records the two release binaries by sha256 and the phase commit" "$(yn bins_in_row)"
      check "$label: the run row's tool_args is $EDIT" "$(yn [ "$args" = "$EDIT" ])"
    done
    check "the same workbooks are refused on both targets, with the same messages (none)" "$(yn cmp -s "$B/refused-host" "$B/refused-i686")"
    cp "$B/refused-host" "$B/c-refused"; printf 'x\tsome message\n' >>"$B/c-refused"
    check "control: the same comparison tells a planted refusal list from the host's" "$(ynnot cmp -s "$B/c-refused" "$B/refused-i686")"
    mkdir -p "$B/c-refrun/r1"
    printf 'error: a planted message\n' >"$B/c-refrun/r1/stderr.host.txt"
    ref_read() { [ "$(refusal_of "$B/c-refrun" r1 host)" = "a planted message" ]; }
    check "control: refusal_of reads a planted refusal's message" "$(yn ref_read)"
    : >"$B/c-refrun/r1/stderr.host.txt"
    ref_none() { [ -z "$(refusal_of "$B/c-refrun" r1 host)" ]; }
    check "control: refusal_of reads nothing from an empty standard error" "$(yn ref_none)"
    entries_ctl() {
      local id
      id=$(head -n 1 "$B/order" | cut -f1)
      printf 'no/such/styles.xml\n0\n' >"$B/c-parts"
      entries_named "$O/entries.host.tsv" "$id" "$B/c-parts"
    }
    check "control: entries_named refuses the first workbook's rows against a styles part it does not hold" "$(ynnot entries_ctl)"
    
    echo
    echo "### the tool lines' totals over the host's ok workbooks, beside the corpus figures FACTS.md carries (printed, not checked; change NSJ)"
    declare -A FACT_OF
    FACT_OF[named]=221; FACT_OF[named_xfs]=459; FACT_OF[builtin]=185; FACT_OF[custom]=71; FACT_OF[dxfs]=1360
    FACT_OF[dxf_fonts]=964; FACT_OF[dxf_fills]=459; FACT_OF[dxf_borders]=260; FACT_OF[dxf_numfmts]=147
    FACT_OF[dxf_alignments]=495; FACT_OF[dxf_protections]=14; FACT_OF[dxf_gradients]=0
    FACT_OF[dxf_implied_solid]=179; FACT_OF[dxf_inside_sides]=164
    n_fact=0; n_fact_same=0
    for k in named named_xfs builtin custom dxfs dxf_fonts dxf_fills dxf_borders dxf_numfmts dxf_alignments dxf_protections dxf_gradients dxf_implied_solid dxf_inside_sides dxf_written dxf_equal; do
      total=$(cut -f2- "$B/lines-host" | tr '\t' '\n' | sed -n "s/^$k=//p" | awk '{ n += $1 } END { print n + 0 }')
      if [ -n "${FACT_OF[$k]:-}" ]; then
        n_fact=$((n_fact + 1))
        if [ "$total" = "${FACT_OF[$k]}" ]; then same=yes; n_fact_same=$((n_fact_same + 1)); else same="no (a finding)"; fi
        echo "  $k: $total; the corpus figure ${FACT_OF[$k]}; the same: $same"
      else
        echo "  $k: $total"
      fi
    done
    echo "  figures the same as FACTS.md's: $n_fact_same of $n_fact"
    
    echo
    echo "### the planted-flag controls, host, each on the first ok workbook in manifest order of the changed case and of the kept case (change NSH)"
    first_case() { awk -F'\t' -v v="$1" '$2 == v { print $1; exit }' "$B/case-host"; }
    CASE_CHANGED=$(first_case changed)
    CASE_KEPT=$(first_case kept)
    echo "  the changed case: ${CASE_CHANGED:-none}; the kept case: ${CASE_KEPT:-none}"
    both_cases() { [ -n "$CASE_CHANGED" ] && [ -n "$CASE_KEPT" ]; }
    check "the corpus gives a changed case and a kept case" "$(yn both_cases)"
    nplants=0; nbit_c=0; nbit_k=0
    for f in $FLAGS; do
      nplants=$((nplants + 1))
      for case in changed kept; do
        if [ "$case" = changed ]; then id=$CASE_CHANGED; else id=$CASE_KEPT; fi
        planted=""
        if [ -n "$id" ]; then
          ext=$(awk -F'\t' -v id="$id" '$1 == id { print $2 }' "$B/order")
          planted=$(python3 "$B/namedcmp.py" namedstyles "$CORPUS/corpus/$id.$ext" "$O/$id/out.host.$ext" --diff "$O/$id/diff.host.tsv" --plant "$f")
        fi
        flag=$f
        turned() { [ -n "$planted" ] && [ "$(kv "$planted" "$flag")" = no ] && [ "$(kv "$planted" planted)" = yes ]; }
        echo "  plant $f on the $case case ${id:-none}: planted=$(kv "$planted" planted); $flag=$(kv "$planted" "$flag")"
        if turned; then
          if [ "$case" = changed ]; then nbit_c=$((nbit_c + 1)); else nbit_k=$((nbit_k + 1)); fi
        fi
        check "control: the plant $f on the $case case turns $flag to no" "$(yn turned)"
      done
    done
    echo "  plants per case: $nplants; that turned their own flag: changed $nbit_c, kept $nbit_k"
    check "every flag has a plant that turned it on the changed case ($nbit_c of $nplants)" "$(yn [ "$nbit_c" = "$nplants" ])"
    check "every flag has a plant that turned it on the kept case ($nbit_k of $nplants)" "$(yn [ "$nbit_k" = "$nplants" ])"
    first_ok=$(head -n 1 "$B/lines-host" | cut -f1)
    first_ext=$(awk -F'\t' -v id="$first_ok" '$1 == id { print $2 }' "$B/order")
    unknown_plant() { [ "$(python3 "$B/namedcmp.py" namedstyles "$CORPUS/corpus/$first_ok.$first_ext" "$O/$first_ok/out.host.$first_ext" --plant no_such_flag)" = error=unknown-plant ]; }
    check "control: the comparison refuses a plant it does not know" "$(yn unknown_plant)"
    
    echo
    echo "### the two labels' outputs"
    same_out=0
    nboth=0
    while IFS="$TAB" read -r id ext; do
      if [ -n "$(awk -F'\t' -v id="$id" '$1 == id' "$B/refused-host")" ]; then continue; fi
      nboth=$((nboth + 1))
      if cmp -s "$O/$id/out.host.$ext" "$O/$id/out.i686.$ext"; then same_out=$((same_out + 1)); else echo "    $id: the outputs differ"; fi
    done <"$B/order"
    echo "  ok workbooks: $nboth; whose host and i686 outputs are byte for byte the same: $same_out"
    check "every output is the same on both targets" "$(yn [ "$same_out" = "$nboth" ])"
    check "both targets printed the same line for every ok workbook" "$(yn cmp -s "$B/lines-host" "$B/lines-i686")"
    cp "$B/lines-host" "$B/c-lines"; printf 'x\n' >>"$B/c-lines"
    check "control: the same comparison tells a line list with one line added" "$(ynnot cmp -s "$B/c-lines" "$B/lines-i686")"
    
    echo
    echo "## the $SAMPLE run's record pair"
    echo "command: scripts/passthrough-record.py --run <runs>/$RUN-$SAMPLE --out <scripts>/out/records --stem $STEM"
    scripts/passthrough-record.py --run "$O" --out "$RECORDS" --stem "$STEM" >"$B/record.out" 2>&1
    rrc=$?
    sed 's/^/    /' "$B/record.out"
    check "the record script exits 0" "$(yn [ "$rrc" = 0 ])"
    RTXT=$RECORDS/$STEM.txt
    RMD=$RECORDS/$STEM.md
    # The families: the names of the host entries table's changed, added and
    # dropped rows, which entries_named checked row by row against the --parts
    # lines above.
    awk -F'\t' 'NR == 1 { for (i = 1; i <= NF; i++) k[$i] = i; next } $k["status"] ~ /^(changed|added|dropped)$/ { print $k["status"] "\t" $k["name"] }' "$O/entries.host.tsv" >"$B/w.parts"
    check "the changed, added and dropped names were read ($(count_lines "$B/w.parts") names)" "$(yn [ "$(count_lines "$B/w.parts")" -ge 1 ])"
    FAM_CHANGED=$(fams_of "$B/w.parts" changed)
    FAM_ADDED=$(fams_of "$B/w.parts" added)
    FAM_DROPPED=$(fams_of "$B/w.parts" dropped)
    echo "  the families: changed ${FAM_CHANGED:-none}; added ${FAM_ADDED:-none}; dropped ${FAM_DROPPED:-none}"
    fams_ok() { [ -n "$FAM_CHANGED" ] && [ -z "$FAM_ADDED$FAM_DROPPED" ]; }
    check "the changed families were derived (some family), none added or dropped" "$(yn fams_ok)"
    python3 "$B/reccheck.py" scripts/passthrough-record.py "$O" "$RTXT" "$RMD" "$FAM_CHANGED" "$FAM_ADDED" "$FAM_DROPPED" "$EDIT" >"$B/reccheck.out" 2>&1
    echo "  exit: $?"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$B/reccheck.out"
    rec_all() { [ "$(count_matches -E ': yes$' "$B/reccheck.out")" = 18 ] && [ "$(count_matches -E ': no$' "$B/reccheck.out")" = 0 ]; }
    check "the record's three tables are the run directory's, and its family tables are counted from them (eighteen checks: four, six per label, two)" "$(yn rec_all)"
    awk '!done && /^[|] total [|]/ { done = 1; next } { print }' "$RMD" >"$B/c-rec.md"
    python3 "$B/reccheck.py" scripts/passthrough-record.py "$O" "$RTXT" "$B/c-rec.md" "$FAM_CHANGED" "$FAM_ADDED" "$FAM_DROPPED" "$EDIT" >"$B/c-reccheck.out" 2>&1
    sed '2d' "$RTXT" >"$B/c-rec.txt"
    python3 "$B/reccheck.py" scripts/passthrough-record.py "$O" "$B/c-rec.txt" "$RMD" "$FAM_CHANGED" "$FAM_ADDED" "$FAM_DROPPED" "$EDIT" >"$B/c-reccheck2.out" 2>&1
    python3 "$B/reccheck.py" scripts/passthrough-record.py "$O" "$RTXT" "$RMD" "$FAM_CHANGED" "$FAM_ADDED" "planted" "$EDIT" >"$B/c-reccheck3.out" 2>&1
    rec_ctl() { [ "$(count_matches -E ': no$' "$B/c-reccheck.out")" -ge 1 ] && [ "$(count_matches -F "the summary table is every label's summary: no" "$B/c-reccheck2.out")" = 1 ]; }
    check "control: the same check finds an .md with a family table's total row dropped and a .txt one summary row short" "$(yn rec_ctl)"
    rec_drop() { [ "$(count_matches -E "the dropped entries' families are planted: no\$" "$B/c-reccheck3.out")" = 2 ]; }
    check "control: the same check finds the dropped families differ from a planted family, on each label" "$(yn rec_drop)"
    check "the record script and the record check left no scripts/__pycache__ (PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE)" "$(yn no_pycache)"
    echo "command: install -m 644 <scripts>/out/records/$STEM.md <scripts>/out/records/$STEM.txt <repo>/$RECORDS_DEST/"
    install -m 644 "$RMD" "$RTXT" "$RECORDS_DEST"/ && INSTALLED+=("$RECORDS_DEST/$STEM.md" "$RECORDS_DEST/$STEM.txt")
    echo "  exit: $?"
    for f in "$STEM.md" "$STEM.txt"; do
      echo "    installed $RECORDS_DEST/$f: sha256 $(sha_of "$RECORDS_DEST/$f"), $(wc -c <"$RECORDS_DEST/$f") bytes, mode $(stat -c %a "$RECORDS_DEST/$f")"
      check "the installed $f is the written one, mode 644" "$(yn inst_same "$f")"
    done
    
    echo
    if [ "$RUN_SKIP_KEEP" = yes ]; then
    echo "## the keep and the open check: SKIPPED (RUN_SKIP_KEEP=yes, a dry run)"
    else
    echo "## the host keep regenerated (change NSF: M3 part 7 P5's form, one cargo test)"
    mkdir "$KEEP" || exit 2
    echo "command: EMEND_KEEP_DIR=<keep> cargo test --workspace (host; CARGO_TARGET_DIR=<target>/main)"
    EMEND_KEEP_DIR=$KEEP cargo test --workspace >"$B/keep.out" 2>&1 </dev/null
    rc=$?
    echo "  exit: $rc"
    LC_ALL=C "$G" -E '^ *Running |^ *Doc-tests |^test result: ' "$B/keep.out" | sed 's/^ */    /'
    failed=$(awk '/^test result: / { for (i = 1; i < NF; i++) if ($(i + 1) ~ /^failed;$/) n += $i } END { print n + 0 }' "$B/keep.out")
    passed=$(awk '/^test result: / { for (i = 1; i < NF; i++) if ($(i + 1) ~ /^passed;$/) n += $i } END { print n + 0 }' "$B/keep.out")
    echo "  passed $passed; failed $failed"
    check "the tests with the keep set exit 0" "$(yn [ "$rc" = 0 ])"
    check "no test failed" "$(yn [ "$failed" = 0 ])"
    echo "  files in the keep: $(find "$KEEP" -type f | wc -l); entries that are not regular files: $(find "$KEEP" -mindepth 1 ! -type f | wc -l)"
    (cd "$KEEP" && find . -mindepth 1 -printf '%P\n' | LC_ALL=C sort) >"$B/host.files"
    nfiles=$(count_lines "$B/host.files")
    n_in=$(count_matches -E '\.in\.xlsx$' "$B/host.files")
    n_out=$(count_matches -E '\.out\.xlsx$' "$B/host.files")
    n_other=$(count_matches -vE '^[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+\.[0-9]+\.(in|out)\.xlsx$' "$B/host.files")
    LC_ALL=C sed -nE 's/^(.*)\.in\.xlsx$/\1/p' "$B/host.files" | LC_ALL=C sort >"$B/pair.names"
    LC_ALL=C sed -nE 's/^(.*)\.out\.xlsx$/\1/p' "$B/host.files" | LC_ALL=C sort >"$B/pair.out.names"
    echo "  .in.xlsx $n_in; .out.xlsx $n_out; names not of the form <test>.<n>.in|out.xlsx: $n_other"
    all_pairs() { [ "$n_in" = "$n_out" ] && [ "$((n_in * 2))" = "$nfiles" ] && [ "$n_other" = 0 ] && cmp -s "$B/pair.names" "$B/pair.out.names"; }
    check "the keep holds only whole pairs named <test>.<n>" "$(yn all_pairs)"
    NPAIRS=$n_in
    (cd "$KEEP" && find . -type f -printf '%P\t%s\n' | LC_ALL=C sort) >"$B/keep.listing"
    echo "  the host keep's listing: pairs $(count_matches -E "[.]in[.]xlsx${TAB}" "$B/keep.listing"); files $(count_lines "$B/keep.listing"); listing sha256 $(sha_of "$B/keep.listing")"
    check "the host keep's pairs times two equals its files (keep_pairs_ok)" "$(yn keep_pairs_ok "$B/keep.listing")"
    
    echo
    echo "## the host keep against M3 part 7 P5's committed open-check record, named by its record commit (change NSF)"
    PREV_TXT=$(git show --name-only --format= "$PREV_OPEN_REC" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -E '^records/[a-z0-9]+-open-.*[.]txt$')
    echo "command: git show --name-only --format= <M3 part 7 P5's record commit>, the open-check .txt it added; git show <phase commit>:<it>"
    echo "  the record: $PREV_TXT (sha256 $(git show "$C:$PREV_TXT" | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1))"
    check "the named record commit added exactly one open-check .txt" "$(yn [ "$(printf '%s\n' "$PREV_TXT" | count_lines /dev/stdin)" = 1 ])"
    no_later_open() { [ -z "$(git log --format=%H "$PREV_OPEN_REC..$C" -- 'records/*-open-*.txt')" ]; }
    check "no commit after it adds an open-check record, so it is the last committed" "$(yn no_later_open)"
    git show "$C:$PREV_TXT" >"$B/prev.txt"
    while IFS= read -r t; do
      printf '%s\t%s\t%s\t%s\t%s\n' "$t" "$(stat -c %s "$KEEP/$t.in.xlsx")" "$(sha_of "$KEEP/$t.in.xlsx")" \
        "$(stat -c %s "$KEEP/$t.out.xlsx")" "$(sha_of "$KEEP/$t.out.xlsx")"
    done <"$B/pair.names" >"$B/keep.rows"
    tail -n +2 "$B/prev.txt" | cut -f1-5 | LC_ALL=C sort >"$B/prev.rows"
    LC_ALL=C sort "$B/keep.rows" >"$B/keep.sorted"
    n_prev=$(count_lines "$B/prev.rows")
    n_kept_prev=$(LC_ALL=C comm -12 "$B/prev.rows" "$B/keep.sorted" | count_lines /dev/stdin)
    cut -f1 "$B/prev.rows" >"$B/prev.names"
    LC_ALL=C comm -13 "$B/prev.names" <(cut -f1 "$B/keep.sorted") >"$B/new.pairs"
    LC_ALL=C comm -23 "$B/prev.names" <(cut -f1 "$B/keep.sorted") >"$B/gone.pairs"
    echo "  rows: the regenerated keep $(count_lines "$B/keep.rows"), the record $n_prev; its rows found in the keep with the same name, bytes and both sha256s: $n_kept_prev"
    echo "  pairs in the keep and not in the record: $(count_lines "$B/new.pairs"); in the record and not in the keep: $(count_lines "$B/gone.pairs")"
    sed 's/^/    new: /' "$B/new.pairs"
    LC_ALL=C comm -23 "$B/prev.rows" "$B/keep.sorted" | cut -f1 >"$B/changed.pairs"
    echo "  pairs of the record whose bytes differ in the keep: $(count_lines "$B/changed.pairs")"
    sed 's/^/    changed: /' "$B/changed.pairs"
    check "no pair of the record is gone" "$(yn [ "$(count_lines "$B/gone.pairs")" = 0 ])"
    check "every pair of the record is in the keep, unchanged or changed ($n_kept_prev + $(count_lines "$B/changed.pairs") = $n_prev)" "$(yn [ "$((n_kept_prev + $(count_lines "$B/changed.pairs")))" = "$n_prev" ])"
    echo "command: the #[test] functions added or whose body is edited since the named record commit, and those of a .rs file whose text outside its tests differs, from the two commits' sources of every .rs file git diff --name-only <named record commit> <phase commit> names: <work>/edited.py, below (change NSG)"
    cat >"$B/edited.py" <<'PY'
    """The #[test] functions whose body differs between two commits, or that
    the second adds: each file's text at both commits (git show), every
    function after a #[test] attribute (other attributes allowed between), its
    body from the fn line to the first line that is a lone closing brace in
    column one. Prints one test name per line; with a third argument
    --fixtures, instead every test whose body names an item (const,
    static, fn, struct, enum, type or mod at column one) whose lines
    outside the test bodies differ between the two commits (change
    NSG)."""
    import collections
    import re
    import subprocess
    import sys
    
    base, head = sys.argv[1:3]
    TEST = re.compile(r"#\[test\]\s*(?:#\[[^\]]*\]\s*)*fn\s+([A-Za-z0-9_]+)")
    
    
    def show(rev, path):
        run = subprocess.run(["git", "show", "%s:%s" % (rev, path)], capture_output=True)
        return run.stdout.decode() if run.returncode == 0 else ""
    
    
    def tests(text):
        out = {}
        for m in TEST.finditer(text):
            end = text.find("\n}\n", m.start())
            out[m.group(1)] = text[m.start():end if end >= 0 else len(text)]
        return out
    
    
    names = subprocess.run(["git", "diff", "--name-only", base, head, "--", "*.rs"],
                           capture_output=True, check=True).stdout.decode().split()
    ITEM = re.compile(r"^(?:pub(?:\([^)]*\))?\s+)?(?:const|static|fn|struct|enum|type|mod)\s+([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)")
    
    
    def outside(text):
        out, at = [], 0
        for m in TEST.finditer(text):
            end = text.find("\n}\n", m.start())
            end = len(text) if end < 0 else end + 3
            if m.start() >= at:
                out.append(text[at:m.start()])
                at = end
        out.append(text[at:])
        return "".join(out)
    
    
    def changed_items(before_text, after_text):
        found = set()
        for text, other in ((after_text, before_text), (before_text, after_text)):
            others = collections.Counter(outside(other).split("\n"))
            current = None
            for line in outside(text).split("\n"):
                m = ITEM.match(line)
                if m:
                    current = m.group(1)
                if others[line] > 0:
                    others[line] -= 1
                elif current is not None:
                    found.add(current)
        return found
    
    
    edited = set()
    fixture = set()
    for path in names:
        before_text, after_text = show(base, path), show(head, path)
        before, after = tests(before_text), tests(after_text)
        for name, body in after.items():
            if before.get(name) != body:
                edited.add(name)
        items = changed_items(before_text, after_text)
        for name, body in after.items():
            if any(re.search(r"\b%s\b" % re.escape(i), body) for i in items):
                fixture.add(name)
    for name in sorted(fixture if sys.argv[3:] == ["--fixtures"] else edited):
        print(name)
    PY
    sed 's/^/    /' "$B/edited.py"
    python3 "$B/edited.py" "$PREV_OPEN_REC" "$C" | LC_ALL=C sort >"$B/edited.tests"
    python3 "$B/edited.py" "$PREV_OPEN_REC" "$C" --fixtures | LC_ALL=C sort >"$B/fixture.tests"
    LC_ALL=C sort -u "$B/edited.tests" "$B/fixture.tests" >"$B/touched.tests"
    sed 's/^/    added or edited test: /' "$B/edited.tests"
    sed 's/^/    test of a file whose text outside its tests differs: /' "$B/fixture.tests"
    sed -E 's/\.[0-9]+$//; s/^.*\.//' "$B/new.pairs" | LC_ALL=C sort -u >"$B/new.tests"
    sed -E 's/\.[0-9]+$//; s/^.*\.//' "$B/changed.pairs" | LC_ALL=C sort -u >"$B/changed.tests"
    echo "  tests with a new pair: $(count_lines "$B/new.tests"); tests with a changed pair: $(count_lines "$B/changed.tests"); tests added or edited: $(count_lines "$B/edited.tests"); tests of a file whose text outside its tests differs: $(count_lines "$B/fixture.tests")"
    check "some test is added or edited, so the list was read" "$(yn [ "$(count_lines "$B/edited.tests")" -ge 1 ])"
    new_from_edited() { [ "$(LC_ALL=C comm -23 "$B/new.tests" "$B/edited.tests" | count_lines /dev/stdin)" = 0 ]; }
    check "every new pair is kept by a test added or edited since the record" "$(yn new_from_edited)"
    changed_from_touched() { [ "$(LC_ALL=C comm -23 "$B/changed.tests" "$B/touched.tests" | count_lines /dev/stdin)" = 0 ]; }
    check "every changed pair of the record is kept by a test edited since it, or of a file whose fixtures or helpers changed (change NSG)" "$(yn changed_from_touched)"
    printf 'zzz_not_an_edited_test\n' | LC_ALL=C sort -m - "$B/new.tests" >"$B/c-new.tests"
    new_ctl() { [ "$(LC_ALL=C comm -23 "$B/c-new.tests" "$B/edited.tests" | count_lines /dev/stdin)" = 1 ]; }
    check "control: the same comparison finds a pair of a test not added or edited" "$(yn new_ctl)"
    printf 'zzz_not_a_touched_test\n' | LC_ALL=C sort -m - "$B/changed.tests" >"$B/c-changed.tests"
    touched_ctl() { [ "$(LC_ALL=C comm -23 "$B/c-changed.tests" "$B/touched.tests" | count_lines /dev/stdin)" = 1 ]; }
    check "control: the same comparison finds a changed pair of a test neither edited nor of a changed file" "$(yn touched_ctl)"
    
    echo
    echo "## scripts/edit-open-check.sh on the host keep (specs/0018 \"Harness runs\": every phase's run log runs it over its keep)"
    mkdir "$B/tmp"
    # The open check's own TMPDIR, its device beside the runs' and the corpus
    # directory's.
    dev_open=$(stat -c %d "$B/tmp")
    echo "command: stat -c %d <work>/tmp <work>/tmp-run <corpus>/corpus /proc"
    echo "  device of the open check's TMPDIR (<work>/tmp): $dev_open; of the runs' TMPDIR (<work>/tmp-run): $(stat -c %d "$RUNTMP"); of the corpus directory (<corpus>/corpus): $dev_corpus; of /proc (the control): $dev_proc"
    check "the open check's TMPDIR and the corpus directory are on one device" "$(yn [ "$dev_open" = "$dev_corpus" ])"
    check "control: the same comparison tells /proc's device from the open check's TMPDIR's" "$(yn [ "$dev_proc" != "$dev_open" ])"
    echo "command: TMPDIR=<work>/tmp scripts/edit-open-check.sh --keep <keep> --libreoffice $IMAGE --out <scripts>/out/records --stem $STEM_OPEN"
    TMPDIR=$B/tmp scripts/edit-open-check.sh --keep "$KEEP" --libreoffice "$IMAGE" --out "$RECORDS" --stem "$STEM_OPEN" \
      >"$B/oc.stdout" 2>"$B/oc.stderr" </dev/null
    oc_rc=$?
    echo "  exit: $oc_rc"
    echo "  stdout:"; sed 's/^/    /' "$B/oc.stdout"
    echo "  stderr bytes: $(wc -c <"$B/oc.stderr")"
    check "the script exits 0 (no finding, no check errored)" "$(yn [ "$oc_rc" = 0 ])"
    check "its stderr is empty" "$(yn [ ! -s "$B/oc.stderr" ])"
    echo "  the reasons the script kept (its reasons directory under <work>/tmp), one line per refused side:"
    find "$B/tmp" -name '*-reason.txt' | LC_ALL=C sort | while IFS= read -r f; do echo "    ${f#"$B/tmp/"}: $(cat "$f")"; done
    TXT=$RECORDS/$STEM_OPEN.txt
    MD=$RECORDS/$STEM_OPEN.md
    TXT_HEADER=$(git show "$C:scripts/edit-open-check.sh" | sed -n "s/^readonly TXT_HEADER=\\$'\\(.*\\)'\$/\\1/p" | sed 's/\\t/\t/g')
    check "the .txt's header is the script's TXT_HEADER, read from the phase commit (nine columns)" "$(yn [ "$(head -n 1 "$TXT")" = "$TXT_HEADER" ])"
    tail -n +2 "$TXT" | cut -f1-5 >"$B/txt.rows"
    nrow_same=$(paste -d'\n' "$B/keep.rows" "$B/txt.rows" | awk 'NR % 2 == 1 { a = $0; next } a == $0 { n++ } END { print n + 0 }')
    echo "  rows: the keep $(count_lines "$B/keep.rows"), the .txt $(count_lines "$B/txt.rows"); rows whose name, bytes and hashes are the keep's, compared row by row: $nrow_same"
    rows_same() { [ "$(count_lines "$B/keep.rows")" = "$(count_lines "$B/txt.rows")" ] && [ "$nrow_same" = "$(count_lines "$B/keep.rows")" ] && [ "$nrow_same" = "$NPAIRS" ]; }
    check "every .txt row is one kept pair's name, byte counts and sha256s, in name order, one row per pair" "$(yn rows_same)"
    bad_rows=$(tail -n +2 "$TXT" | awk -F'\t' 'NF != 9 || $6 !~ /^(ok|fail|error)$/ || $7 !~ /^(ok|fail|error)$/ || $8 !~ /^(none|refused|count|error)$/ || $9 !~ /^(none|refused|count|error)$/' | wc -l)
    check "every row has nine columns, lo_in and lo each ok, fail or error, and each class none, refused, count or error ($bad_rows rows otherwise)" "$(yn [ "$bad_rows" = 0 ])"
    bad_fit=$(tail -n +2 "$TXT" | awk -F'\t' '{ print $6 ":" $8; print $7 ":" $9 }' | LC_ALL=C "$G" -cvxE 'ok:none|fail:refused|fail:count|error:error')
    check "every side's class fits its verdict ($bad_fit sides otherwise)" "$(yn [ "$bad_fit" = 0 ])"
    stdout_rows() { [ "$(awk -F'\t' 'NF == 3' "$B/oc.stdout")" = "$(tail -n +2 "$TXT" | cut -f1,6,7)" ]; }
    check "the script's per-pair stdout lines are the .txt's test, lo_in and lo columns" "$(yn stdout_rows)"
    echo "command: python3 <work>/wb.py over each kept input: its xl/workbook.xml entry, its sheet elements by local name (expat, no pattern) and of them those with a prefix"
    cat >"$B/wb.py" <<'PY'
    import sys, zipfile
    from xml.parsers import expat
    for path in sys.argv[1:]:
        name = path.rsplit("/", 1)[1][: -len(".in.xlsx")]
        try:
            z = zipfile.ZipFile(path)
        except zipfile.BadZipFile:
            print("%s\tunreadable\t-\t-" % name)
            continue
        if "xl/workbook.xml" not in z.namelist():
            print("%s\tno\t-\t-" % name)
            continue
        found = {"all": 0, "prefixed": 0}
    
        def start(tag, attrs):
            prefix, _, local = tag.rpartition(":")
            if local == "sheet":
                found["all"] += 1
                found["prefixed"] += 1 if prefix else 0
        p = expat.ParserCreate()
        p.StartElementHandler = start
        try:
            p.Parse(z.read("xl/workbook.xml"), True)
        except expat.ExpatError:
            print("%s\tyes\tunparsed\t-" % name)
            continue
        print("%s\tyes\t%d\t%d" % (name, found["all"], found["prefixed"]))
    PY
    sed 's/^/    /' "$B/wb.py"
    python3 "$B/wb.py" $(sed "s#^#$KEEP/#; s#\$#.in.xlsx#" "$B/pair.names") | LC_ALL=C sort >"$B/wb.all"
    echo "  kept inputs by workbook entry and sheet elements (entry, all, prefixed: pairs):"
    cut -f2- "$B/wb.all" | sort | uniq -c | sed 's/^/    /'
    echo "  the .md checked against the .txt and the kept inputs, with the heading specs/0015 P2 verification ruling 1 gives: <work>/mdcheck.py, below"
    cat >"$B/mdcheck.py" <<'PY'
    import sys
    txt, md, wb = sys.argv[1:4]
    rows = [l.split("\t") for l in open(txt).read().split("\n")[1:] if l]
    sheets = {l.split("\t")[0]: l.split("\t")[2] for l in open(wb).read().split("\n") if l}
    text = open(md).read().split("\n")
    REFUSED = ("Inputs refused by LibreOffice (allowed: a fixture LibreOffice cannot load: zip-level,"
               " or a package with no relationships part or an empty content-types root)")
    
    
    def section(title):
        out, on = [], False
        for line in text:
            if line == "## " + title:
                on = True
                continue
            if on and line.startswith("## "):
                break
            if on and line:
                out.append(line)
        return out
    
    
    def listed(names):
        return ["- `%s`" % n for n in names] if names else ["None."]
    
    
    def count(col, v):
        return sum(1 for r in rows if r[col] == v)
    
    
    totals = [len(rows)] + [count(5, v) for v in ("ok", "fail", "error")] + [count(6, v) for v in ("ok", "fail", "error")]
    classes = ["| %s | " % side + " | ".join(str(count(col, c)) for c in ("none", "refused", "count", "error")) + " |"
               for side, col in (("reason_in", 7), ("reason_out", 8))]
    tot = section("Totals")
    checks = [
        ("Totals", tot[2:3] == ["| " + " | ".join(str(t) for t in totals) + " |"] and tot[5:] == classes),
        ("the refused-inputs heading reads as ruled, once", text.count("## " + REFUSED) == 1),
        ("Inputs refused by LibreOffice", section(REFUSED) == listed([r[0] for r in rows if r[7] == "refused"])),
        ("the sheet count did not apply", section("Inputs the sheet count did not apply to (allowed: a workbook fixture with no sheet element)") == listed([r[0] for r in rows if r[7] == "count" and sheets.get(r[0]) == "0"])),
        ("counts differ", section("Inputs whose sheet and table counts differ (a finding)") == listed([r[0] for r in rows if r[7] == "count" and sheets.get(r[0]) != "0"])),
        ("Outputs refused on an accepted input", section("Outputs refused on an input LibreOffice accepted (a finding)") == listed([r[0] for r in rows if r[6] == "fail" and r[5] == "ok"])),
        ("Checks that did not run", section("Checks that did not run (error)") == listed([r[0] for r in rows if "error" in (r[5], r[6])])),
        ("Pairs", section("Pairs")[2:] == ["| `%s` | %s | %s | %s | %s | %s | %s | %s | %s |" % tuple(r) for r in rows]),
        ("the Pairs line", ("- Pairs: %d" % len(rows)) in text),
    ]
    for name, ok in checks:
        print("%s: %s" % (name, "yes" if ok else "no"))
    print("totals: pairs %d; lo_in ok %d fail %d error %d; lo ok %d fail %d error %d" % tuple(totals))
    PY
    sed 's/^/    /' "$B/mdcheck.py"
    python3 "$B/mdcheck.py" "$TXT" "$MD" "$B/wb.all" >"$B/mdcheck.out"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$B/mdcheck.out"
    md_all() { [ "$(count_matches -E ': yes$' "$B/mdcheck.out")" = 9 ] && [ "$(count_matches -E ': no$' "$B/mdcheck.out")" = 0 ]; }
    check "the .md's nine parts are derived from the .txt and the kept inputs' sheet elements, the heading as ruled" "$(yn md_all)"
    head -n 2 "$TXT" >"$B/c-short.txt"
    python3 "$B/mdcheck.py" "$B/c-short.txt" "$MD" "$B/wb.all" >"$B/c-mdcheck.out"
    md_ctl() { [ "$(count_matches -E ': no$' "$B/c-mdcheck.out")" -ge 1 ]; }
    check "control: the same check on a .txt cut to one row finds the .md does not match it" "$(yn md_ctl)"
    OLD8=records/m1p8-open-2026-09-24-da080f1
    python3 "$B/mdcheck.py" "$OLD8.txt" "$OLD8.md" "$B/wb.all" >"$B/c-prevmd.out"
    old_heading() { [ "$(count_matches -F 'the refused-inputs heading reads as ruled, once: no' "$B/c-prevmd.out")" = 1 ]; }
    check "control: the same check on part 8 P2's committed .md finds the old heading, not the ruled one" "$(yn old_heading)"
    totals_line() { [ "$(sed -n 's/^wrote .*\.txt: \(pairs [^;]*; lo_in [^;]*; lo [^;]*\); inputs refused .*/\1/p' "$B/oc.stdout")" = "$(sed -n 's/^totals: //p' "$B/mdcheck.out")" ]; }
    check "the script's totals line is the totals derived from the .txt" "$(yn totals_line)"
    echo
    echo "### the verdicts against the named record"
    join -t "$TAB" <(tail -n +2 "$B/prev.txt" | cut -f1,6,7,8,9 | LC_ALL=C sort) <(tail -n +2 "$TXT" | cut -f1,6,7,8,9 | LC_ALL=C sort) >"$B/both"
    check "every pair of the named record has a row in this record" "$(yn [ "$(count_lines "$B/both")" = "$n_prev" ])"
    awk -F'\t' '$2 != $6 || $3 != $7 || $4 != $8 || $5 != $9 { print $1 "\t" $2 "/" $3 "/" $4 "/" $5 " -> " $6 "/" $7 "/" $8 "/" $9 }' "$B/both" >"$B/moved"
    echo "  the named record's pairs whose lo_in, lo or either class changed: $(count_lines "$B/moved")"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$B/moved"
    check "no verdict and no class of the named record's pairs moved" "$(yn [ "$(count_lines "$B/moved")" = 0 ])"
    printf 'x\tok\tok\tnone\tnone\tok\tfail\tnone\trefused\n' >"$B/c-both"
    moved_ctl() { [ "$(awk -F'\t' '$2 != $6 || $3 != $7 || $4 != $8 || $5 != $9' "$B/c-both" | wc -l)" = 1 ]; }
    check "control: the same form finds a planted row whose lo moved" "$(yn moved_ctl)"
    echo "  the new pairs' verdicts (test, lo_in, lo, reason_in, reason_out):"
    join -t "$TAB" "$B/new.pairs" <(tail -n +2 "$TXT" | cut -f1,6,7,8,9 | LC_ALL=C sort) | sed 's/^/    /'
    no_new_finding() { [ "$(join -t "$TAB" "$B/new.pairs" <(tail -n +2 "$TXT" | cut -f1,6,7 | LC_ALL=C sort) | awk -F'\t' '$2 == "ok" && $3 != "ok"' | wc -l)" = 0 ]; }
    check "no new pair's output is refused on an accepted input" "$(yn no_new_finding)"
    echo
    echo "### acceptance, and the inputs LibreOffice did not accept"
    tail -n +2 "$TXT" | awk -F'\t' -v OFS='\t' '{ print ($1 ~ /^emend-copy\./ ? "tool" : "crate"), $1, $6, $7, $8, $9 }' >"$B/verdicts"
    for side in crate tool; do
      n=$(awk -F'\t' -v s="$side" '$1 == s' "$B/verdicts" | wc -l)
      nfind=$(awk -F'\t' -v s="$side" '$1 == s && $3 == "ok" && $4 == "fail"' "$B/verdicts" | wc -l)
      nerr=$(awk -F'\t' -v s="$side" '$1 == s && ($3 == "error" || $4 == "error")' "$B/verdicts" | wc -l)
      nin=$(awk -F'\t' -v s="$side" '$1 == s && $3 == "fail"' "$B/verdicts" | wc -l)
      echo "  $side: pairs $n; inputs refused $nin; outputs refused on an accepted input $nfind; checks that did not run $nerr"
      check "$side: no output refused on an accepted input" "$(yn [ "$nfind" = 0 ])"
      check "$side: no check errored" "$(yn [ "$nerr" = 0 ])"
    done
    awk -F'\t' '$5 == "count" { print $2 }' "$B/verdicts" >"$B/count.pairs"
    awk -F'\t' '$2 == "yes" && $3 == "0" { print $1 }' "$B/wb.all" >"$B/zero.pairs"
    echo "  count-class inputs $(count_lines "$B/count.pairs"); kept inputs with a workbook entry and no sheet element $(count_lines "$B/zero.pairs")"
    check "the count-class inputs are exactly the kept inputs with a workbook entry and no sheet element, so no count differs" "$(yn cmp -s "$B/count.pairs" "$B/zero.pairs")"
    echo "  the pairs whose input LibreOffice did not accept, with the class of the input's reason:"
    awk -F'\t' '$3 != "ok" { print $2 "\t" $5 }' "$B/verdicts" | sed 's/^/    /'
    echo
    echo "### the open-check record installed into records/"
    echo "command: install -m 644 <scripts>/out/records/$STEM_OPEN.md <scripts>/out/records/$STEM_OPEN.txt <repo>/$RECORDS_DEST/"
    install -m 644 "$RECORDS/$STEM_OPEN.md" "$RECORDS/$STEM_OPEN.txt" "$RECORDS_DEST"/ && INSTALLED+=("$RECORDS_DEST/$STEM_OPEN.md" "$RECORDS_DEST/$STEM_OPEN.txt")
    echo "  exit: $?"
    for f in "$STEM_OPEN.md" "$STEM_OPEN.txt"; do
      echo "    written <scripts>/out/records/$f: sha256 $(sha_of "$RECORDS/$f"), $(wc -c <"$RECORDS/$f") bytes"
      echo "    installed $RECORDS_DEST/$f: sha256 $(sha_of "$RECORDS_DEST/$f"), $(wc -c <"$RECORDS_DEST/$f") bytes, mode $(stat -c %a "$RECORDS_DEST/$f")"
      check "the installed $f is the written one, byte for byte, mode 644" "$(yn inst_same "$f")"
    done
    fi
    
    echo
    echo "## the record files this run installed hold no path"
    echo "  record files installed by this run: ${#INSTALLED[@]}"
    no_path() {
      local f
      [ "${#INSTALLED[@]}" -ge 1 ] || return 1
      for f in "${INSTALLED[@]}"; do
        [ "$(count_matches -F "$HOME" "$f")" = 0 ] || return 1
        [ "$(count_matches -E '(/home/|/mnt/|/Users/|/tmp/|emend-testing)' "$f")" = 0 ] || return 1
      done
    }
    check "no record file this run installed names <home>, a home, mount, temporary or corpus path" "$(yn no_path)"
    n_inst_want=4
    if [ "$RUN_SKIP_KEEP" = yes ]; then n_inst_want=2; fi
    check "this run installed the record files it writes ($n_inst_want: the run pair, and the open pair unless the keep was skipped)" "$(yn [ "${#INSTALLED[@]}" = "$n_inst_want" ])"
    printf '%s%s%s\n' '/ho' 'me/someone/' 'emend-testing/corpus/x' >"$B/c-path"
    path_ctl() { [ "$(count_matches -E '(/home/|/mnt/|/Users/|/tmp/|emend-testing)' "$B/c-path")" = 1 ]; }
    check "control: the same form finds a planted path" "$(yn path_ctl)"
    
    echo
    echo "## status after the run"
    echo "command: git status --porcelain"
    git status --porcelain | sed 's/^/    /'
    st_all=$(run_lines git status --porcelain)
    st_ours=$(run_matches -E "$OURS" git status --porcelain)
    echo "  planning's uncommitted spec: $SPEC, sha256 $(sha_of "$SPEC")"
    echo "status lines: $st_all; of them this phase's logs, its record pairs or planning's uncommitted spec: $st_ours"
    status_accounted() { [ "$st_all" != error ] && [ "$st_ours" != error ] && [ "$st_all" = "$st_ours" ]; }
    check "every change in the working tree is this phase's or planning's uncommitted spec" "$(yn status_accounted)"
    echo
    echo "## this script's own standard error (specs/0017 P1 verification ruling 7)"
    nerr=$(wc -c <"$ERR")
    cp "$ERR" "$B/c-err"; printf 'x' >>"$B/c-err"
    nerr_ctl=$(wc -c <"$B/c-err")
    echo "  command: wc -c <scripts>/out/run.stderr: $nerr bytes; a copy with one byte appended: $nerr_ctl"
    check "this script wrote nothing to its standard error" "$(yn [ "$nerr" = 0 ])"
    check "control: the same count reads one byte more in the copy" "$(yn [ "$nerr_ctl" = "$((nerr + 1))" ])"
    echo "run ended at $(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)"
    echo "run log checks all as expected: $([ "$fail" -eq 0 ] && echo yes || echo no)"
    exec 1>&3
    wait "$SCRUB_PID" 2>/dev/null
    exit "$fail"

## the shared counting library this log sources (the phase commit's, by git show; change NSB)
    # emend shared counting forms (specs/0007-gate-self-test.md, "scripts/counting.sh").
    #
    # Sourced by scripts/gate-self-test.sh and by the log scripts of later phases,
    # which use these instead of carrying their own copy.
    #
    # WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. In T3 P4 four counting sites compared a bare `grep -c`
    # with 0 without reading the exit status, so a read error printed 0 and the
    # check passed. Two independent checks found them, and the class was declared
    # closed three further times while instances still stood: a helper whose first
    # repair read grep's status while `cat` was the failing command, and both
    # halves of one function in T2 P7. Planning's remedy is that every counting
    # form, including a throwaway one, is a named function that reads the exit
    # status and has a positive control, from the start.
    #
    # Every function prints either a number or the word "error". None of them ever
    # prints a matched line, a value, or a path. A caller that compares a result
    # with 0 therefore cannot mistake a failed read for an absence.
    #
    # counting_controls runs every form against a match, a miss and an unreadable
    # file, prints one line per control, and sets counting_controls_ok. Callers run
    # it before using any form.
    
    G=/usr/bin/grep
    
    # count_matches <-F|-E> <pattern> <file>...: total matching lines across the
    # files, or "error" if any file could not be read. The files go to grep
    # directly: with `cat file | grep -c`, an unreadable file makes CAT fail while
    # grep counts 0 over the empty stream and exits 1, so the read error reads as
    # "no hits".
    count_matches() {
      local mode=$1 pattern=$2 out rc
      shift 2
      out=$(LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -H -c "$mode" -e "$pattern" -- "$@" 2>/dev/null); rc=$?
      if [ "$rc" -ge 2 ]; then printf 'error'; return; fi
      printf '%s\n' "$out" | awk -F: '{ n += $NF } END { print n + 0 }'
    }
    
    # count_from_file <-F|-E> <pattern file> <file>...: the same, with the patterns
    # read from a file (grep -f), so a pattern is never printed.
    count_from_file() {
      local mode=$1 patterns=$2 out rc
      shift 2
      out=$(LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -H -c "$mode" -f "$patterns" -- "$@" 2>/dev/null); rc=$?
      if [ "$rc" -ge 2 ]; then printf 'error'; return; fi
      printf '%s\n' "$out" | awk -F: '{ n += $NF } END { print n + 0 }'
    }
    
    # count_bytes <tr class> <file>...: total bytes of that class across the files,
    # or "error" if any file could not be read. Each file is read on its own rather
    # than through `cat "$@" | tr`, for the same reason as above.
    count_bytes() {
      local class=$1 total=0 f n
      shift
      for f in "$@"; do
        [ -r "$f" ] || { printf 'error'; return; }
        n=$(LC_ALL=C tr -cd "$class" <"$f" | wc -c) || { printf 'error'; return; }
        total=$((total + n))
      done
      printf '%s' "$total"
    }
    
    # count_lines <file>...: total lines, or "error" if any file could not be read.
    count_lines() {
      local total=0 f n
      for f in "$@"; do
        [ -r "$f" ] || { printf 'error'; return; }
        n=$(wc -l <"$f") || { printf 'error'; return; }
        total=$((total + n))
      done
      printf '%s' "$total"
    }
    
    # count_matches_i <-F|-E> <pattern> <file>...: count_matches with -i, the form
    # the hygiene step uses for OFFICE_RE and ZONE_RE. It lived in a log script as a
    # hand-rolled copy with no control of its own (independent check 2, T6 P1, gap
    # 14); a counting form belongs here, with a control, even a throwaway one.
    count_matches_i() {
      local mode=$1 pattern=$2 out rc
      shift 2
      out=$(LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -H -c -i "$mode" -e "$pattern" -- "$@" 2>/dev/null); rc=$?
      if [ "$rc" -ge 2 ]; then printf 'error'; return; fi
      printf '%s\n' "$out" | awk -F: '{ n += $NF } END { print n + 0 }'
    }
    
    # run_lines <command...>: run the command, and print the number of lines it
    # wrote on stdout, or "error" if the command itself failed. The log scripts
    # asserted a clean working tree with
    #   git status --porcelain >file 2>/dev/null || : >file
    # which turns a FAILED git status into an empty file, so the check read a
    # failed command as a clean tree (independent check 2, T6 P1, gap 1; planning
    # reproduced it). Reading the command's exit status is the whole point: a
    # command that could not run is never the same as a command that found nothing.
    run_lines() {
      local out rc
      out=$("$@" 2>/dev/null); rc=$?
      if [ "$rc" -ne 0 ]; then printf 'error'; return; fi
      if [ -z "$out" ]; then printf '0'; return; fi
      printf '%s\n' "$out" | wc -l | tr -d ' '
    }
    
    # run_matches <-F|-E> <pattern> <command...>: the same, counting only the lines
    # that match, so a caller can compare "all lines" with "lines of the expected
    # shape" without either count hiding a failed command.
    run_matches() {
      local mode=$1 pattern=$2 out rc
      shift 2
      out=$("$@" 2>/dev/null); rc=$?
      if [ "$rc" -ne 0 ]; then printf 'error'; return; fi
      if [ -z "$out" ]; then printf '0'; return; fi
      printf '%s\n' "$out" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -c "$mode" -e "$pattern" || true
    }
    
    CTRL_CLASS='\000-\010\013\014\016-\037\177'
    NONASCII_CLASS='\200-\377'
    
    # counting_controls <label prefix>: run every counting form above against a
    # fixture that must match and one that must not, and against an unreadable
    # file, printing one line per result. Sets counting_controls_ok to yes or no.
    # This is the positive control planning requires for every form, and it also
    # proves each form reports "error" rather than 0 when it cannot read.
    counting_controls() {
      local d ok=yes r
      d=$(mktemp -d) || { counting_controls_ok=no; return; }
      printf 'alpha\nbeta needle gamma\nneedle\n' >"$d/hit"
      printf 'nothing of interest\n' >"$d/miss"
      printf 'x \033[31mred\033[m\017 y\ncaf\303\251\n' >"$d/bytes"
      printf 'needle\n' >"$d/patterns"
      printf 'unreadable\n' >"$d/locked"
      chmod 000 "$d/locked"
    
      r=$(count_matches -F needle "$d/hit");        echo "  control count_matches on a file with two matching lines: $r (expect 2)"; [ "$r" = 2 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_matches -F needle "$d/miss");       echo "  control count_matches on a file with none: $r (expect 0)"; [ "$r" = 0 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_matches -F needle "$d/hit" "$d/miss"); echo "  control count_matches summed over two files: $r (expect 2)"; [ "$r" = 2 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_matches -E 'ne+dle' "$d/hit");      echo "  control count_matches with a regular expression: $r (expect 2)"; [ "$r" = 2 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_matches -F needle "$d/locked");     echo "  control count_matches on an unreadable file: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_matches -F needle "$d/hit" "$d/locked"); echo "  control count_matches on readable plus unreadable: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_from_file -F "$d/patterns" "$d/hit"); echo "  control count_from_file on the same file: $r (expect 2)"; [ "$r" = 2 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_from_file -F "$d/patterns" "$d/miss"); echo "  control count_from_file on a file with none: $r (expect 0)"; [ "$r" = 0 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_from_file -F "$d/patterns" "$d/locked"); echo "  control count_from_file on an unreadable file: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_bytes "$CTRL_CLASS" "$d/bytes");    echo "  control count_bytes, control bytes in a file with ESC, ESC and SI: $r (expect 3)"; [ "$r" = 3 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_bytes "$NONASCII_CLASS" "$d/bytes"); echo "  control count_bytes, non-ASCII bytes in a file with one two-byte character: $r (expect 2)"; [ "$r" = 2 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_bytes "$CTRL_CLASS" "$d/miss");     echo "  control count_bytes on a clean file: $r (expect 0)"; [ "$r" = 0 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_bytes "$CTRL_CLASS" "$d/locked");   echo "  control count_bytes on an unreadable file: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_lines "$d/hit");                    echo "  control count_lines on a three-line file: $r (expect 3)"; [ "$r" = 3 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_lines "$d/locked");                 echo "  control count_lines on an unreadable file: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      printf 'NEEDLE\nneedle\n' >"$d/mixedcase"
      r=$(count_matches_i -F needle "$d/mixedcase"); echo "  control count_matches_i on mixed case: $r (expect 2)"; [ "$r" = 2 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_matches -F needle "$d/mixedcase");  echo "  control count_matches on the same file, case sensitive: $r (expect 1)"; [ "$r" = 1 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_matches_i -F needle "$d/locked");   echo "  control count_matches_i on an unreadable file: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      r=$(run_lines printf 'a\nb\nc\n');            echo "  control run_lines on a command printing three lines: $r (expect 3)"; [ "$r" = 3 ] || ok=no
      r=$(run_lines true);                          echo "  control run_lines on a command printing nothing: $r (expect 0)"; [ "$r" = 0 ] || ok=no
      r=$(run_lines false);                         echo "  control run_lines on a FAILING command: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      r=$(run_lines "$d/no-such-command");          echo "  control run_lines on a command that cannot run: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      r=$(run_matches -F needle printf 'needle\nother\n'); echo "  control run_matches on a command printing one match: $r (expect 1)"; [ "$r" = 1 ] || ok=no
      r=$(run_matches -F needle false);             echo "  control run_matches on a FAILING command: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
    
      chmod 644 "$d/locked"
      rm -rf "${d:?}"
      counting_controls_ok=$ok
      echo "  counting controls: $([ "$ok" = yes ] && echo "all as expected" || echo FAILED)"
    }

